00:25:02.130 --> 00:25:04.050
of the same corporate donors,

586
00:25:04.050 --> 00:25:06.140
whether it has to do with the military-industrial complex,

587
00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:09.540
whether it has to do with big pharmaceutical companies,

588
00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:10.960
fossil fuel companies,

589
00:25:10.960 --> 00:25:13.090
big agricultural companies,

590
00:25:13.090 --> 00:25:14.623
big chemical companies,

591
00:25:15.720 --> 00:25:16.553
not the NRA.

592
00:25:18.020 --> 00:25:19.290
On that one, they are better,

593
00:25:19.290 --> 00:25:21.190
but they're still not getting it done.

594
00:25:22.420 --> 00:25:24.780
We all need to awaken (snaps).

595
00:25:24.780 --> 00:25:26.510
It's like a woman who...

596
00:25:26.510 --> 00:25:30.050
Her friends just have to say, "Honey, he's a bad guy.

597
00:25:30.050 --> 00:25:31.370
He's not who you think he is."

598
00:25:31.370 --> 00:25:33.900
At this point, these people are not doing it,

599
00:25:33.900 --> 00:25:35.400
because they do not choose to.

600
00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:38.370
Yeah, it was fascinating

601
00:25:38.370 --> 00:25:43.370
to observe during your presidential bit

602
00:25:44.240 --> 00:25:48.030
how the media treated you so unfairly,

603
00:25:48.030 --> 00:25:50.000
the manner in which you were marginalized.

604
00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:52.250
And I mentioned earlier I had Andrew Yang in here,

605
00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:53.960
and he shared a little bit

606
00:25:53.960 --> 00:25:56.330
about his personal experience with that,

607
00:25:56.330 --> 00:25:59.427
which was a lesser version of what you experienced,

608
00:25:59.427 --> 00:26:02.940
and he wrote quite extensively about it in his book.

609
00:26:02.940 --> 00:26:05.410
But it was quite disheartening

610
00:26:05.410 --> 00:26:07.920
to see the manner

611
00:26:07.920 --> 00:26:12.920
in which you were maligned and made fun of and marginalized

612
00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:19.000
when your debate performances

613
00:26:19.240 --> 00:26:23.420
created so much conversation and a lotta interest.

614
00:26:23.420 --> 00:26:28.120
And yet you would read the pieces about those performances,

615
00:26:28.120 --> 00:26:30.450
and they were written with such a tone

616
