and the things that are true about me that are not perfect,

804
00:33:41.010 --> 00:33:42.610
character defects, whatever.

805
00:33:42.610 --> 00:33:43.730
I thought those would come up,

806
00:33:43.730 --> 00:33:46.360
but this mischaracterization of wacky girl

807
00:33:46.360 --> 00:33:47.620
who doesn't go to the doctor

808
00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:50.380
and doesn't believe disease is real, what?

809
00:33:50.380 --> 00:33:52.840
So I take responsibility.

810
00:33:52.840 --> 00:33:54.730
That's number one, and number two,

811
00:33:54.730 --> 00:33:58.130
what I knew I had to do was clear all that,

812
00:33:58.130 --> 00:34:00.723
and that's what that year was about for me.

813
00:34:01.790 --> 00:34:03.270
It's true. It's a cliche, but it's true.

814
00:34:03.270 --> 00:34:05.560
You get bitter, or you get better.

815
00:34:05.560 --> 00:34:07.020
Had to forgive myself.

816
00:34:07.020 --> 00:34:08.193
Have to forgive others.

817
00:34:10.300 --> 00:34:14.740
I didn't wanna go forward with a chip on my shoulder.

818
00:34:14.740 --> 00:34:16.390
We all fall down in life,

819
00:34:16.390 --> 00:34:21.320
but I think the issue is who gets back up and how.

820
00:34:21.320 --> 00:34:22.830
Hemingway said, "Everybody's"...

821
00:34:22.830 --> 00:34:23.663
What'd he say?

822
00:34:23.663 --> 00:34:25.010
"Everybody's broken, but some grow stronger

823
00:34:25.010 --> 00:34:26.340
at the broken places"?

824
00:34:26.340 --> 00:34:30.030
So the issue for me is can I be a truth-teller

825
00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:32.300
and point out what I think needs to be pointed out

826
00:34:32.300 --> 00:34:33.610
without playing violence

827
00:34:33.610 --> 00:34:35.480
like, "Poor me. What they did to me,"

828
00:34:35.480 --> 00:34:38.150
because what they did to me is small

829
00:34:38.150 --> 00:34:40.140
compared to the larger issue of what's being done

830
00:34:40.140 --> 00:34:42.250
to the planet and to people all over the world.

831
00:34:42.250 --> 00:34:47.010
Yeah, I just remember you being on the stage

832
00:34:47.010 --> 00:34:51.760
and just very bluntly speaking truth to power

833
00:34:51.760 --> 00:34:56.180
in a manner that was very bold and extremely unusual,

834
00:34:56.180 --> 00:34:59.586
perhaps unprecedented for that type of dais,

835
00:34:59.586 --> 00:35:00.907
(chuckles) to just say,

836
00:35:00.907 --> 00:35:03.440
"Look, we gotta confront the dark with the light,"

837
00:35:03.440 --> 00:35:07.390
and in a very matter-of-fact and convicted way,

838
00:35:07.390 --> 00:35:11.017
and I think that's why you ended up getting googled so much:

839
00:35:11.017 --> 00:35:13.620
"Holy shit, I've never seen anything like this before.

840
00:35:13.620 --> 00:35:15.280
What are we gonna do with this?"

841
00:35:15.280 --> 00:35:16.970
Well, the DNC had ideas

842
00:35:16.970 --> 00:35:18.601
around that, of course.
Yeah, oh yeah, that though.

843
00:35:18.601 --> 00:35:22.360
But I look at it as almost as if...

844
00:35:23.610 --> 00:35:25.440
Listen, you knew

845
00:35:25.440 --> 00:35:27.910
you weren't gonna win the presidency, right?

846
00:35:27.910 --> 00:35:30.410
It's almost as if you were this Trojan horse

847
00:35:30.410 --> 00:35:33.550
like, "I'm gonna insert myself into this equation,

848
00:35:33.550 --> 00:35:38.000
and I'm going to seed the national dialogue

849
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:40.670
with certain ideas

850
00:35:40.670 --> 00:35:44.610
that I think are hyper-relevant,

851
00:35:44.610 --> 00:35:48.420
and I know that I'm gonna be perhaps mocked for them."

852
00:35:48.420 --> 00:35:49.667
I did know. (scoffs)

853
00:35:49.667 --> 00:35:52.077
"But I'm opening the door for the next person," right?

854
00:35:52.077 --> 00:35:55.430
"I'm creating permission

855
00:35:55.430 --> 00:35:59.290
so that this is can actually occur in the future."

856
00:35:59.290 --> 00:36:04.250
It's like you were the courageous adventurer,

857
00:36:04.250 --> 00:36:06.297
the first person to say,

858
00:36:06.297 --> 00:36:08.180
"Let's talk about this more broadly.

859
00:36:08.180 --> 00:36:09.070
Let's talk about this

860
00:36:09.070 --> 00:36:12.830
from a broader, spiritual perspective,"

861
00:36:12.830 --> 00:36:16.450
in a situation in which we have the Democratic Party

862
00:36:16.450 --> 00:36:19.160
that has abdicated any relationship

863
00:36:19.160 --> 00:36:23.990
with anything spiritual or religious in any regard.

864
00:36:23.990 --> 00:36:28.640
That's been monopolized by the right in a certain way

865
00:36:28.640 --> 00:36:31.700
and has left the Democratic Party fearful

866
00:36:31.700 --> 00:36:35.550
of even talking about these things in a meaningful way.

867
00:36:35.550 --> 00:36:36.853
I dunno about fearful.

868
00:36:37.880 --> 00:36:40.503
I think that by surrendering,

869
00:36:42.690 --> 00:36:45.390
we just abdicated the moral conversation.

870
00:36:45.390 --> 00:36:48.380
Traditionally, on the political right,

871
00:36:48.380 --> 00:36:50.840
they talked about issues of private morality,

872
00:36:50.840 --> 00:36:52.160
and on their political left,

873
00:36:52.160 --> 00:36:53.670
there were issues of public morality.

874
00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:57.270
War and peace should be seen as a moral issue.

875
00:36:57.270 --> 00:36:58.410
Whether you invade and country

876
00:36:58.410 --> 00:36:59.810
that didn't do anything to you

877
00:36:59.810 --> 00:37:01.350
is a moral issue.

878
00:37:01.350 --> 00:37:04.450
Economic justice should be seen as a moral issue,

879
00:37:04.450 --> 00:37:06.080
but over the last few decades...

880
00:37:06.080 --> 00:37:07.810
And I don't even know how it happened.

881
00:37:07.810 --> 00:37:09.430
Bobby Kennedy said

882
00:37:09.430 --> 00:37:13.070
that the contest was for the soul of America.

883
00:37:13.070 --> 00:37:14.730
JFK said, "We can't afford

884
00:37:14.730 --> 00:37:17.500
to be materially rich and spiritually poor."

885
00:37:17.500 --> 00:37:18.660
When I was growing up

886
00:37:18.660 --> 00:37:23.110
during the anti-war movements of the 1960s and '70s,

887
00:37:23.110 --> 00:37:25.980
Reverend William Sloane Coffin, the Berrigan brothers,

888
00:37:25.980 --> 00:37:28.110
there was definitely a religious left,

889
00:37:28.110 --> 00:37:29.860
so this is an aberration

890
00:37:29.860 --> 00:37:32.830
that the left in America has become so overly secularized,

891
00:37:32.830 --> 00:37:34.130
but I'd like to go back for a moment

892
00:37:34.130 --> 00:37:36.397
to something you just said about...

893
00:37:36.397 --> 00:37:38.747
"You opened the conversation."

894
00:37:38.747 --> 00:37:40.620
"Oh, you brought up the conversation."

895
00:37:40.620 --> 00:37:42.200
You know what? Lemme tell you something.

896
00:37:42.200 --> 00:37:47.200
We don't have time left to just influence the conversation,

897
00:37:47.550 --> 00:37:49.490
so yes, in my campaign,

898
00:37:49.490 --> 00:37:50.877
hopefully, I did what you said,

899
00:37:50.877 --> 00:37:53.720
"Opened the door," "next person," et cetera,

900
00:37:53.720 --> 00:37:56.150
but this idea...

901
00:37:56.150 --> 00:37:57.560
Sometimes people say, "Oh, Marianne,

902
00:37:57.560 --> 00:38:00.490
you really influenced the consciousness of people."

903
00:38:00.490 --> 00:38:02.840
The consciousness of people is not the problem.

904
00:38:04.110 --> 00:38:05.510
That's not where the problem lies.

905
00:38:05.510 --> 00:38:08.752
The problem lies is in those who are holding the levers

906
00:38:08.752 --> 00:38:11.030
of political and economic power.

907
00:38:11.030 --> 00:38:12.500
I have had the experience

908
00:38:12.500 --> 00:38:15.680
of, quote, unquote, "advising" the most powerful people

909
00:38:15.680 --> 00:38:16.560
in the country.

910
00:38:16.560 --> 00:38:19.440
It's too late to just advise them.

911
00:38:19.440 --> 00:38:21.510
We need to replace them,

912
00:38:21.510 --> 00:38:24.743
so that goes back to this whole issue of incrementalism.

913
00:38:25.840 --> 00:38:28.440
You don't go through a situation

914
00:38:28.440 --> 00:38:31.520
as brutal as running for president

915
00:38:31.520 --> 00:38:33.740
only wanting to influence the conversation,

916
00:38:33.740 --> 00:38:35.040
not that I thought

917
00:38:35.040 --> 00:38:37.060
that I would become president

918
00:38:37.060 --> 00:38:38.053
in that election.

919
00:38:40.268 --> 00:38:43.323
If somebody is sending you money to support your campaign,

920
00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:47.520
even if it's $10,

921
00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:49.850
you have, I think, an ethical responsibility

922
00:38:49.850 --> 00:38:52.070
to play it as seriously as you can,

923
00:38:52.070 --> 00:38:52.903
and I tried.

924
00:38:53.890 --> 00:38:56.293
The fact that I, in moments of nervousness,

925
00:38:58.090 --> 00:39:01.130
sounded silly clearly was used

926
00:39:01.130 --> 00:39:06.040
by those who sought to mock me,

927
00:39:06.040 --> 00:39:08.090
but once again, that's my responsibility.

928
00:39:09.860 --> 00:39:10.693
I own it.

929
00:39:11.670 --> 00:39:14.240
You've spoken many times

930
00:39:14.240 --> 00:39:19.240
about the legacy and the impact of Bobby Kennedy and MLK

931
00:39:19.900 --> 00:39:24.390
and what their assassinations meant

932
00:39:24.390 --> 00:39:27.233
in terms of the chilling effect on activism,

933
00:39:28.390 --> 00:39:33.390
this sense that we can be active or raise our voices

934
00:39:34.020 --> 00:39:35.630
only to a certain degree

935
00:39:36.470 --> 00:39:39.400
but that the powers that be are going to ensure

936
00:39:39.400 --> 00:39:44.400
that that pressure valve gets released a little bit,

937
00:39:44.510 --> 00:39:49.510
but as long as you go back and become a quiet citizen.

938
00:39:50.120 --> 00:39:53.480
How do you reconcile that,

939
00:39:53.480 --> 00:39:58.480
this idea, "okay, in the private sphere, go consume.

940
00:39:59.140 --> 00:40:00.087
Do whatever you want.

941
00:40:00.087 --> 00:40:03.040
And the public sphere, leave that to us"?

942
00:40:03.040 --> 00:40:06.320
Here we are in a very precarious situation.

943
00:40:06.320 --> 00:40:07.713
Can that be changed?

944
00:40:08.570 --> 00:40:11.460
What you're saying, I think, is so important,

945
00:40:11.460 --> 00:40:13.360
and as someone who lived through that,

946
00:40:14.580 --> 00:40:17.590
the Kennedys, Dr. King,

947
00:40:17.590 --> 00:40:20.070
the people who were holding aloft

948
00:40:20.070 --> 00:40:21.700
the highest aspirations

949
00:40:21.700 --> 00:40:24.220
philosophically, morally, spiritually,

950
00:40:24.220 --> 00:40:29.220
were being channeled within a political context.

951
00:40:31.369 --> 00:40:34.710
They were older than the youth movement at that time.

952
00:40:34.710 --> 00:40:38.000
They were literally shot and killed in front of our eyes,

953
00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:41.363
and it was very clear that the message was for all of us.

954
00:40:42.450 --> 00:40:45.740
Those bullets psychically shot all of us.

955
00:40:45.740 --> 00:40:47.817
It was a very loud unspoken message:

956
00:40:47.817 --> 00:40:49.870
"There will be no further protest.

957
00:40:49.870 --> 00:40:50.960
You will go home.

958
00:40:50.960 --> 00:40:52.540
You will do whatever you want in the private sector.

959
00:40:52.540 --> 00:40:54.260
You'll have a lotta choice, lotta choice.

960
00:40:54.260 --> 00:40:55.750
You can have the yellow one. You could buy the blue one.

961
00:40:55.750 --> 00:40:58.260
You can buy the red one. So much choice,"

962
00:40:58.260 --> 00:41:00.130
and just in case we didn't get the message,

963
00:41:00.130 --> 00:41:01.880
they killed the kids at Kent State.

964
00:41:04.160 --> 00:41:07.720
We all did as we were told, but you know what?

965
00:41:07.720 --> 00:41:09.170
Something has changed now

966
00:41:09.170 --> 00:41:11.490
because that generation that was young then

967
00:41:11.490 --> 00:41:13.000
has become older now,

968
00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:16.600
and today, I know for myself

969
00:41:16.600 --> 00:41:19.100
and I think for a lotta people in my generation,

970
00:41:19.100 --> 00:41:21.350
the idea that we might die knowing in our hearts

971
00:41:21.350 --> 00:41:24.800
that "the bastard got to us," as my father would say,

972
00:41:24.800 --> 00:41:26.370
knowing in our hearts we didn't really do

973
00:41:26.370 --> 00:41:28.560
what we came here to do in this lifetime

974
00:41:28.560 --> 00:41:31.130
is actually scarier to us

975
00:41:31.130 --> 00:41:34.510
than the thought that they might kill us if we do.

976
00:41:34.510 --> 00:41:39.040
Now, you have tremendous, I believe, political potential

977
00:41:40.160 --> 00:41:43.020
in harnessing the impulses

978
00:41:43.020 --> 00:41:45.260
of those who are still young enough to dream,

979
00:41:45.260 --> 00:41:47.260
and those who are experienced or old enough

980
00:41:47.260 --> 00:41:49.240
to have now become wise.

981
00:41:49.240 --> 00:41:51.330
I have never seen anything...

982
00:41:51.330 --> 00:41:53.760
I don't think there's been in American history

983
00:41:53.760 --> 00:41:56.270
like the way the U.S. government

984
00:41:56.270 --> 00:42:00.133
collectively and systemically abuses our young.

985
00:42:01.100 --> 00:42:03.550
It is unbelievable.

986
00:42:03.550 --> 00:42:05.300
Between the college-loan debt,

987
00:42:05.300 --> 00:42:06.770
the lack of health care,

988
00:42:06.770 --> 00:42:09.660
the lack of availability of free education,

989
00:42:09.660 --> 00:42:12.110
it's like instead of saying, "Hey, kids,"

990
00:42:12.110 --> 00:42:13.327
like we would as parents,

991
00:42:13.327 --> 00:42:15.010
"this country should not be run as a business.

992
00:42:15.010 --> 00:42:18.080
This country should be run like a family.

993
00:42:18.080 --> 00:42:20.040
We're gonna give you everything possible

994
00:42:20.040 --> 00:42:21.110
so that you can go out there

995
00:42:21.110 --> 00:42:22.350
and you can thrive and make it,

996
00:42:22.350 --> 00:42:23.620
and we're gonna hold you accountable,

997
00:42:23.620 --> 00:42:26.240
but we're gonna give you all the tools of success,"

998
00:42:26.240 --> 00:42:28.723
we thwart the dreams of our young.

999
00:42:31.210 --> 00:42:35.010
Where I see hope is how many young people really are...

1000
00:42:35.010 --> 00:42:36.210
They don't wanna take anymore.

1001
00:42:36.210 --> 00:42:37.520
They look at global capitalism,

1002
00:42:37.520 --> 00:42:40.190
and they say, "What has global capitalism ever done for me?"

1003
00:42:40.190 --> 00:42:42.217
and they look at socialism, and they go,

1004
00:42:42.217 --> 00:42:43.760
"What should I be so afraid of?

1005
00:42:43.760 --> 00:42:46.037
The free health care? Or the free college?"

1006
00:42:47.450 --> 00:42:49.070
The unfettered...

1007
00:42:50.670 --> 00:42:54.130
The whole orgy of deregulation that began in the 1980s

1008
00:42:54.130 --> 00:42:56.390
so that this shadow side,

1009
00:42:56.390 --> 00:43:00.260
the most irresponsible, amoral strain

1010
00:43:00.260 --> 00:43:02.750
of unfettered, unregulated capitalism

1011
00:43:02.750 --> 00:43:05.120
is now holding this...

1012
00:43:05.120 --> 00:43:06.820
The chokehold it has on the young,

1013
00:43:06.820 --> 00:43:09.280
the chokehold it has on our democracy,

1014
00:43:09.280 --> 00:43:11.370
you have young people who are just...

1015
00:43:11.370 --> 00:43:13.100
They're ready to break through this.

1016
00:43:13.100 --> 00:43:15.027
You have older people who are like,

1017
00:43:15.027 --> 00:43:17.530
"I'm not gonna die without weighing in on this,"

1018
00:43:17.530 --> 00:43:22.530
and we need to harness the political potential

1019
00:43:22.640 --> 00:43:26.690
of the dreamers and the wise.

1020
00:43:26.690 --> 00:43:28.440
Yeah, very well said.

1021
00:43:28.440 --> 00:43:31.250
That pendulum is definitely swinging back

1022
00:43:31.250 --> 00:43:34.000
from the Gordon Gekko "greed is good,"

1023
00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:35.749
rugged individualism, "me, me, me."

1024
00:43:35.749 --> 00:43:37.400
The rugged became rugged narcissism.

1025
00:43:37.400 --> 00:43:41.140
Yeah, we're reaping the havoc

1026
00:43:41.140 --> 00:43:42.960
of too many decades of that,

1027
00:43:42.960 --> 00:43:44.808
and we have these young people who...

1028
00:43:44.808 --> 00:43:45.810
(chuckles) You're very, right?

1029
00:43:45.810 --> 00:43:47.447
It's like, "Seriously?"

1030
00:43:47.447 --> 00:43:49.340
(scoffs) Yeah.

1031
00:43:49.340 --> 00:43:52.410
Not only is higher education restricted.

1032
00:43:52.410 --> 00:43:54.280
It's impossibly expensive.

1033
00:43:54.280 --> 00:43:55.910
I'll be saddled with debt

1034
00:43:55.910 --> 00:43:57.380
and then enter a job market

1035
00:43:57.380 --> 00:44:01.060
where there's no real legitimate opportunities

1036
00:44:01.060 --> 00:44:03.600
to move upward.

1037
00:44:03.600 --> 00:44:04.750
What are the options?

1038
00:44:04.750 --> 00:44:08.340
Right, and so these kids take out these college loans

1039
00:44:08.340 --> 00:44:10.910
in order to get an advanced degree

1040
00:44:10.910 --> 00:44:12.370
in the field that they want to pursue,

1041
00:44:12.370 --> 00:44:15.090
but then they actually can't take a job in that field

1042
00:44:15.090 --> 00:44:18.570
because they will not get the benefits that they need,

1043
00:44:18.570 --> 00:44:20.033
health care, et cetera.

1044
00:44:22.920 --> 00:44:24.450
They need to take the jobs that they hate

1045
00:44:24.450 --> 00:44:26.480
in order to ever pay back the college loans

1046
00:44:26.480 --> 00:44:28.277
which theoretically were giving them the education

1047
00:44:28.277 --> 00:44:29.880
for the life that they want.

1048
00:44:29.880 --> 00:44:32.870
Yeah, I feel a certain

1049
00:44:35.026 --> 00:44:40.026
(tuts) sense of urgent activism and energy that they have.

1050
00:44:40.490 --> 00:44:44.010
You talk about the aging up of the boomers

1051
00:44:44.010 --> 00:44:47.180
and their relationship with the legacy of activism

1052
00:44:47.180 --> 00:44:51.590
and Martin Luther King and Bobby Kennedy, et cetera,

1053
00:44:51.590 --> 00:44:53.560
and this sense of unfulfilled destiny

1054
00:44:53.560 --> 00:44:57.343
in terms of like manifesting the promise of that era,

1055
00:44:58.610 --> 00:45:02.200
but I see young people who are picking up that cause

1056
00:45:02.200 --> 00:45:04.060
and are not taking any bullshit.

1057
00:45:04.060 --> 00:45:04.893
Absolutely-

1058
00:45:04.893 --> 00:45:07.230
And you see that the protests at COP26-

1059
00:45:07.230 --> 00:45:09.730
That's what I was just gonna mention.

1060
00:45:09.730 --> 00:45:12.980
It was a perfect embodiment, what happened in Glasgow,

1061
00:45:12.980 --> 00:45:15.920
the people holding the power inside the building

1062
00:45:15.920 --> 00:45:17.710
were the incrementalists, were the apologists.

1063
00:45:17.710 --> 00:45:18.880
The greenwashing.

1064
00:45:18.880 --> 00:45:20.730
Yeah, and then you had hundreds of thousands,

1065
00:45:20.730 --> 00:45:22.550
or at least over 100,000,

1066
00:45:22.550 --> 00:45:23.770
of people on the street.

1067
00:45:23.770 --> 00:45:25.570
That's where the energy's going.

1068
00:45:25.570 --> 00:45:28.740
The issue is how fast and how much humans...

1069
00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:30.090
The issue is, number one,

1070
00:45:30.090 --> 00:45:32.030
will we be able to pull it off in time.

1071
00:45:32.030 --> 00:45:33.223
Number two (sighs)...

1072
00:45:37.280 --> 00:45:39.027
Sometimes, people say to me,

1073
00:45:39.027 --> 00:45:41.920
"Marianne don't worry about the Earth.

1074
00:45:41.920 --> 00:45:43.310
Don't worry about the environment,

1075
00:45:43.310 --> 00:45:45.423
because worse comes to worst,

1076
00:45:47.110 --> 00:45:50.020
Mother Nature will just have to kick off the planet

1077
00:45:50.020 --> 00:45:51.370
this predatory species

1078
00:45:53.040 --> 00:45:56.530
for 200,000-300,000 years, ha ha,

1079
00:45:56.530 --> 00:45:58.680
so the Earth will be okay,"

1080
00:45:58.680 --> 00:46:01.560
but I think we need to allow ourselves

1081
00:46:01.560 --> 00:46:04.230
to imagine the horror

1082
00:46:04.230 --> 00:46:06.690
of the amount of human and other-species suffering

1083
00:46:06.690 --> 00:46:08.860
that would result from that scenario.

1084
00:46:08.860 --> 00:46:12.100
Something fierce has to arise in us now,

1085
00:46:12.100 --> 00:46:13.853
You're a parent. I'm a parent.

1086
00:46:15.240 --> 00:46:17.483
There's something that happens,

1087
00:46:18.800 --> 00:46:20.010
usually when they're teenagers.

1088
00:46:20.010 --> 00:46:22.270
Usually, it involves sex or drugs.

1089
00:46:22.270 --> 00:46:25.800
There's fierce "that will not be happening in this house,"

1090
00:46:25.800 --> 00:46:27.750
and you don't even necessarily know what you would do

1091
00:46:27.750 --> 00:46:29.020
if they pushed you at that point,

1092
00:46:29.020 --> 00:46:29.900
but they're not gonna push you

1093
00:46:29.900 --> 00:46:32.130
because the look on your face is so serious.

1094
00:46:32.130 --> 00:46:33.947
That's how we have to become:

1095
00:46:33.947 --> 00:46:35.977
"That will not happen."

1096
00:46:37.140 --> 00:46:42.140
I do believe in my heart there are more lovers than haters.

1097
00:46:42.620 --> 00:46:45.070
There are more people yearning

1098
00:46:45.070 --> 00:46:48.170
for the good and the merciful and the humble and the true

1099
00:46:49.020 --> 00:46:51.460
and the beautiful and the democratic,

1100
00:46:51.460 --> 00:46:53.390
but there's a line in "The Course in Miracles"

1101
00:46:53.390 --> 00:46:55.840
where it says, "Miracles arise from conviction."

1102
00:46:55.840 --> 00:46:58.090
Conviction is a force multiplier,

1103
00:46:58.090 --> 00:47:00.440
so more people in this country and in this world

1104
00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:01.990
love than hate,

1105
00:47:01.990 --> 00:47:03.940
but those who hate, the bigots,

1106
00:47:03.940 --> 00:47:06.980
the racists, the antisemites,

1107
00:47:06.980 --> 00:47:10.550
the homophobes, the Islamophobes, they're convicted.

1108
00:47:10.550 --> 00:47:12.890
The terrorists, they are convicted.

1109
00:47:12.890 --> 00:47:13.850
I can't imagine

1110
00:47:13.850 --> 00:47:16.860
a kinda-sorta-sometimes-when-it's-convenient committed

1111
00:47:16.860 --> 00:47:20.173
terrorist or Proud Boy,

1112
00:47:21.310 --> 00:47:23.980
but too many of us who love

1113
00:47:23.980 --> 00:47:27.190
are willing to stand for our love on Tuesdays and Thursdays

1114
00:47:27.190 --> 00:47:28.590
between 2:00 and 4:00,

1115
00:47:28.590 --> 00:47:29.840
and I think people need to realize

1116
00:47:29.840 --> 00:47:32.850
you can't really wage a revolution over white wine and brie.

1117
00:47:32.850 --> 00:47:36.590
We have to become as convicted behind our love

1118
00:47:36.590 --> 00:47:38.700
as some people are convicted behind our hate.

1119
00:47:38.700 --> 00:47:42.060
If you have 10 people who hate with conviction

1120
00:47:42.060 --> 00:47:44.770
and 100 people who love but

1121
00:47:48.014 --> 00:47:51.700
with weak musculature, weak conviction,

1122
00:47:51.700 --> 00:47:55.223
then the conviction will carry the day.

1123
00:47:56.070 --> 00:47:58.167
Vladimir Lenin was asked,

1124
00:47:58.167 --> 00:48:00.550
"How are you going to be able to pull this off?

1125
00:48:00.550 --> 00:48:03.660
How are you ever going to be able to convince the peasants?"

1126
00:48:03.660 --> 00:48:06.750
He said, "I don't need to convince the majority.

1127
00:48:06.750 --> 00:48:09.700
I need 10 good men who understand what I'm talking about."

1128
00:48:09.700 --> 00:48:14.130
I think that we get too concerned about the majority,

1129
00:48:14.130 --> 00:48:16.120
and when you're too concerned about the majority,

1130
00:48:16.120 --> 00:48:18.290
you're willing to dumb down your message

1131
00:48:18.290 --> 00:48:20.480
because you think that social change occurs

1132
00:48:20.480 --> 00:48:22.430
on the horizontal axis.

1133
00:48:22.430 --> 00:48:26.250
I think social change now occurs on the vertical axis.

1134
00:48:26.250 --> 00:48:27.083
Go deep

1135
00:48:27.083 --> 00:48:28.420
with what's true.
It's always operated

1136
00:48:28.420 --> 00:48:29.713
that way.

1137
00:48:29.713 --> 00:48:31.360
And that's why the abolitionists won.

1138
00:48:31.360 --> 00:48:33.540
That's why the civil rights movement prevailed.

1139
00:48:33.540 --> 00:48:36.320
That's why suffragettes won,

1140
00:48:36.320 --> 00:48:39.770
but we need to step up our conviction.

1141
00:48:39.770 --> 00:48:43.780
It's my sense, Rich, that enough of us get it.

1142
00:48:43.780 --> 00:48:45.170
Enough people get it.

1143
00:48:45.170 --> 00:48:47.160
It's not like people are stupid.

1144
00:48:47.160 --> 00:48:49.250
And I found out as a candidate

1145
00:48:49.250 --> 00:48:52.380
the system was even more corrupt than I knew.

1146
00:48:52.380 --> 00:48:54.670
People were even more wonderful and intelligent

1147
00:48:54.670 --> 00:48:56.460
than I hoped for,

1148
00:48:56.460 --> 00:49:00.763
but we have to stand for what we know now and courageously,

1149
00:49:02.390 --> 00:49:05.303
and we'll be able to pull this off.

1150
00:49:06.610 --> 00:49:07.640
I certainly believe

1151
00:49:07.640 --> 00:49:10.820
that love is a more powerful force than hate,

1152
00:49:10.820 --> 00:49:13.580
but there is something very particular about hate

1153
00:49:13.580 --> 00:49:17.150
that lends itself to that level of conviction.

1154
00:49:17.150 --> 00:49:19.320
Hate is a very innervating

1155
00:49:19.320 --> 00:49:20.153
emotional state.
Adrenaline.

1156
00:49:20.153 --> 00:49:21.520
It's an agitation

1157
00:49:22.634 --> 00:49:26.950
that compels somebody

1158
00:49:26.950 --> 00:49:28.270
into a state of conviction,

1159
00:49:28.270 --> 00:49:30.520
whereas love doesn't really operate that way.

1160
00:49:31.572 --> 00:49:34.070
How do you function convicted around love?

1161
00:49:34.070 --> 00:49:36.270
I can understand being convicted

1162
00:49:36.270 --> 00:49:38.610
about justice or truth

1163
00:49:38.610 --> 00:49:41.170
or the difference between right and wrong,

1164
00:49:41.170 --> 00:49:44.270
but love is so much more...

1165
00:49:44.270 --> 00:49:46.313
It's elusive in that regard.

1166
00:49:47.670 --> 00:49:49.310
What is the fulcrum

1167
00:49:49.310 --> 00:49:53.490
that can create that situation

1168
00:49:53.490 --> 00:49:55.760
as a counterbalance to the amount

1169
00:49:55.760 --> 00:49:58.223
of convicted hate that we're seeing?

1170
00:49:59.320 --> 00:50:01.670
I'm not sure I see it totally the same way.

1171
00:50:01.670 --> 00:50:03.280
Look how you love your wife.

1172
00:50:03.280 --> 00:50:05.290
Look how you love your children.

1173
00:50:05.290 --> 00:50:07.640
It's not elusive or effusive.

1174
00:50:07.640 --> 00:50:11.130
It's fierce, but we need to...

1175
00:50:11.130 --> 00:50:12.593
When you learn history,

1176
00:50:13.670 --> 00:50:15.770
when you read American history,

1177
00:50:15.770 --> 00:50:17.040
when you read the history of Europe,

1178
00:50:17.040 --> 00:50:19.240
when you read the history of World War II,

1179
00:50:19.240 --> 00:50:22.180
you learn to have a fire in your belly

1180
00:50:22.180 --> 00:50:25.600
about freedom and about liberty and about democracy.

1181
00:50:25.600 --> 00:50:27.063
This is serious stuff.

1182
00:50:29.380 --> 00:50:32.700
There's such a failure of our educational system.

1183
00:50:32.700 --> 00:50:35.103
If you look at the Declaration of Independence,

1184
00:50:36.200 --> 00:50:38.763
those principles are a mission statement,

1185
00:50:39.970 --> 00:50:41.770
and what has happened

1186
00:50:41.770 --> 00:50:45.120
is that they have become emotionally eroded.

1187
00:50:45.120 --> 00:50:47.190
They're still written on marble walls,

1188
00:50:47.190 --> 00:50:48.830
and they're written on parchment,

1189
00:50:48.830 --> 00:50:51.800
and we hold it behind glass at the Smithsonian or whatever,

1190
00:50:51.800 --> 00:50:55.357
but too many generations have lost their moral force.

1191
00:50:55.357 --> 00:50:57.040
"All men are created equal."

1192
00:50:57.040 --> 00:50:58.700
We have to love that the way

1193
00:50:58.700 --> 00:51:01.630
we love our lovers, our spouses, our children,

1194
00:51:01.630 --> 00:51:03.070
that all men are created equal,

1195
00:51:03.070 --> 00:51:05.810
and all men have the inalienable rights

1196
00:51:05.810 --> 00:51:07.330
given by God

1197
00:51:07.330 --> 00:51:09.270
to life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness,

1198
00:51:09.270 --> 00:51:12.480
that governments are instituted to secure those rights,

1199
00:51:12.480 --> 00:51:14.670
and if government is not doing that job,

1200
00:51:14.670 --> 00:51:17.230
we have the right to alter it or abolish it.

1201
00:51:17.230 --> 00:51:18.063
I love that.

1202
00:51:18.063 --> 00:51:20.773
I love it just like I love a lover or a child.

1203
00:51:23.480 --> 00:51:25.210
To me, that's not elusive,

1204
00:51:25.210 --> 00:51:27.333
and that's why we have to teach our children.

1205
00:51:28.520 --> 00:51:30.010
And I also see it as the difference

1206
00:51:30.010 --> 00:51:32.653
between adrenaline and healthy food.

1207
00:51:33.920 --> 00:51:35.080
That's a good analogy.

1208
00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:38.880
Yeah, if anger is the motivating force

1209
00:51:38.880 --> 00:51:40.150
behind your activism,

1210
00:51:40.150 --> 00:51:41.460
it's like an adrenaline high.

1211
00:51:41.460 --> 00:51:43.780
It's a sugar high, and then you crash.

1212
00:51:43.780 --> 00:51:46.000
This is a marathon, guys.

1213
00:51:46.000 --> 00:51:47.230
But it's addictive too.

1214
00:51:47.230 --> 00:51:49.411
There's a dopamine hit with it.

1215
00:51:49.411 --> 00:51:51.540
(tuts) But as you well know,

1216
00:51:51.540 --> 00:51:52.780
your own work,

1217
00:51:52.780 --> 00:51:54.230
when you do eat healthy food,

1218
00:51:56.430 --> 00:51:59.000
it becomes its own driving force.

1219
00:51:59.000 --> 00:52:00.930
But it's a slower,

1220
00:52:00.930 --> 00:52:01.947
more gentle-
Yeah, it's slower,

1221
00:52:01.947 --> 00:52:03.950
but over time it gives you more energy,

1222
00:52:03.950 --> 00:52:05.870
and it gives you more peace than you realize.

1223
00:52:05.870 --> 00:52:07.343
But it's a process.

1224
00:52:08.520 --> 00:52:09.990
How do you think

1225
00:52:09.990 --> 00:52:13.470
about the role of spirituality in politics?

1226
00:52:13.470 --> 00:52:14.570
You mentioned earlier...

1227
00:52:14.570 --> 00:52:19.040
We were talking about how the Democratic Party has abdicated

1228
00:52:19.040 --> 00:52:20.380
any relationship with this

1229
00:52:20.380 --> 00:52:24.093
and is very secular in the way it conducts itself,

1230
00:52:25.420 --> 00:52:28.490
but the truth is most people have some form

1231
00:52:28.490 --> 00:52:31.453
of spiritual or religious life,

1232
00:52:33.230 --> 00:52:35.513
whether you're on the left or the right.

1233
00:52:42.710 --> 00:52:47.710
There's a religiosity to certain factions of the right,

1234
00:52:48.230 --> 00:52:50.920
but there is no real meaningful dialogue

1235
00:52:50.920 --> 00:52:53.010
around spirituality in politics.

1236
00:52:53.010 --> 00:52:56.360
These things are seen to be separate entities,

1237
00:52:56.360 --> 00:53:00.160
and part of your messaging or your ethos

1238
00:53:00.160 --> 00:53:02.620
is that these are the same thing.

1239
00:53:02.620 --> 00:53:04.070
We need an injection

1240
00:53:04.070 --> 00:53:08.270
of higher consciousness and spiritual awareness

1241
00:53:08.270 --> 00:53:09.260
in our politics.

1242
00:53:09.260 --> 00:53:11.240
If we wanna solve these problems.

1243
00:53:11.240 --> 00:53:13.620
First of all, there's a profound misunderstanding

1244
00:53:13.620 --> 00:53:17.720
of the whole concept of the separation of church and state.

1245
00:53:17.720 --> 00:53:19.160
The separation of church and state

1246
00:53:19.160 --> 00:53:20.940
is one of the most enlightened aspects

1247
00:53:20.940 --> 00:53:22.600
of the U.S. constitution,

1248
00:53:22.600 --> 00:53:26.960
but it was not instituted by our founders

1249
00:53:26.960 --> 00:53:29.030
to suppress the religious impulse.

1250
00:53:29.030 --> 00:53:31.720
It was instituted to protect it.

1251
00:53:31.720 --> 00:53:33.640
It has a dual function.

1252
00:53:33.640 --> 00:53:37.380
On one hand, it means that when Congress is meeting,

1253
00:53:37.380 --> 00:53:40.587
no minister, priest, rabbi, imam, ayatollah

1254
00:53:41.826 --> 00:53:42.890
is gonna walk in there

1255
00:53:42.890 --> 00:53:44.780
and say you can't pass this law

1256
00:53:44.780 --> 00:53:46.420
or you have to pass that law,

1257
00:53:46.420 --> 00:53:48.700
so it protects the government from interference

1258
00:53:48.700 --> 00:53:50.200
by religious authorities.

1259
00:53:50.200 --> 00:53:51.620
But it also means

1260
00:53:51.620 --> 00:53:53.350
that in this country,

1261
00:53:53.350 --> 00:53:56.310
no policeman or policewoman is gonna come

1262
00:53:56.310 --> 00:54:01.240
into a church, a mosque, a synagogue,

1263
00:54:01.240 --> 00:54:03.940
or an atheist meeting,

1264
00:54:03.940 --> 00:54:06.340
because religious freedom means not only the freedom

1265
00:54:06.340 --> 00:54:07.830
to worship as you wish

1266
00:54:07.830 --> 00:54:09.990
but whether or not you wish.

1267
00:54:09.990 --> 00:54:11.447
As Thomas Jefferson said,

1268
00:54:11.447 --> 00:54:14.020
"Whether a man believes in 20 gods or no gods

1269
00:54:14.020 --> 00:54:16.440
neither picks my pocket nor breaks my leg,"

1270
00:54:16.440 --> 00:54:18.020
so no one is going to be told

1271
00:54:18.020 --> 00:54:19.713
by governmental authorities,

1272
00:54:21.079 --> 00:54:24.130
"You cannot pray if you wish and how you wish."

1273
00:54:24.130 --> 00:54:26.040
So they weren't trying to shut people up.

1274
00:54:26.040 --> 00:54:28.750
They were trying to make sure that people were protected.

1275
00:54:28.750 --> 00:54:30.770
Now, that's the first thing,

1276
00:54:30.770 --> 00:54:33.940
that you don't give up your right as a citizen

1277
00:54:33.940 --> 00:54:35.130
to have an opinion

1278
00:54:35.130 --> 00:54:36.950
if your convictions are based

1279
00:54:38.170 --> 00:54:41.290
on spiritual or religious principles.

1280
00:54:41.290 --> 00:54:45.130
The over-secularization of the American left

1281
00:54:45.130 --> 00:54:50.130
has made too many people who do have religious convictions,

1282
00:54:50.210 --> 00:54:52.540
which is the majority of Americans, by the way,

1283
00:54:52.540 --> 00:54:56.450
feel that such thinking is unsophisticated,

1284
00:54:56.450 --> 00:54:59.450
it doesn't belong in the public realm,

1285
00:54:59.450 --> 00:55:01.010
and you need to shut up about it.

1286
00:55:01.010 --> 00:55:04.930
This has had very deleterious effects on American politics,

1287
00:55:04.930 --> 00:55:07.490
particularly for the left.

1288
00:55:07.490 --> 00:55:08.760
Now, if you look...

1289
00:55:08.760 --> 00:55:11.457
Go back to the Declaration of Independence,

1290
00:55:11.457 --> 00:55:16.457
"all men are created equal,

1291
00:55:16.670 --> 00:55:21.240
given by God the inalienable rights

1292
00:55:21.240 --> 00:55:23.470
of life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness."

1293
00:55:23.470 --> 00:55:25.010
On my Substack just last night

1294
00:55:25.010 --> 00:55:27.440
I published an article about abortion.

1295
00:55:27.440 --> 00:55:30.430
I'm very much pro-choice,

1296
00:55:30.430 --> 00:55:31.820
but I'm not pro-choice

1297
00:55:32.912 --> 00:55:36.140
with this idea that it's not a moral issue.

1298
00:55:36.140 --> 00:55:37.800
I think it's very much a moral issue,

1299
00:55:37.800 --> 00:55:40.210
but I trust the moral decision-making

1300
00:55:40.210 --> 00:55:41.540
of the American woman,

1301
00:55:41.540 --> 00:55:44.990
and I don't believe that the government should weigh in

1302
00:55:44.990 --> 00:55:48.240
on somebody's private moral decisions,

1303
00:55:48.240 --> 00:55:50.870
but those people who, over the last few years,

1304
00:55:50.870 --> 00:55:53.320
have deemed themselves arbiters

1305
00:55:53.320 --> 00:55:55.960
of the way Roe V. Wade could be discussed

1306
00:55:55.960 --> 00:55:58.400
have acted like any admission

1307
00:55:58.400 --> 00:56:01.060
that there's even a moral dimension to this question

1308
00:56:01.060 --> 00:56:03.500
would lead to political disaster.

1309
00:56:03.500 --> 00:56:05.740
I think the fact that we have failed

1310
00:56:05.740 --> 00:56:07.350
to contextualize it morally

1311
00:56:07.350 --> 00:56:11.790
is what has led to political disaster

1312
00:56:11.790 --> 00:56:13.370
such as we're experiencing now.

1313
00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:17.270
I think it's been a gift to the anti-choice movement,

1314
00:56:17.270 --> 00:56:19.270
and like I said, there used to be a religious left.

1315
00:56:19.270 --> 00:56:20.500
Today, if you are...

1316
00:56:21.860 --> 00:56:26.860
The black churches have never separated progressive politics

1317
00:56:27.630 --> 00:56:30.610
from religion and spirituality,

1318
00:56:30.610 --> 00:56:33.330
but anyone else is deemed...

1319
00:56:34.830 --> 00:56:37.180
(tuts) We're not supposed to be allowed to say it.

1320
00:56:37.180 --> 00:56:42.180
Sure, there's this coastal elite denigration

1321
00:56:42.910 --> 00:56:45.640
of anything religious or spiritual

1322
00:56:45.640 --> 00:56:48.670
where people who feel strongly

1323
00:56:48.670 --> 00:56:51.490
about their particular vein of faith

1324
00:56:51.490 --> 00:56:56.490
feel; misrepresented's the wrong word;

1325
00:56:56.850 --> 00:57:00.240
dismissed or condescend to.
Yeah, people don't like

1326
00:57:00.240 --> 00:57:01.413
to feel patronized.

1327
00:57:04.600 --> 00:57:07.790
I'm somebody who's been sober for a long time.

1328
00:57:07.790 --> 00:57:09.980
I got sober and stay sober

1329
00:57:09.980 --> 00:57:12.790
in the construct of 12 step,

1330
00:57:12.790 --> 00:57:17.790
and I always tend to evaluate problems and problem-solving

1331
00:57:17.900 --> 00:57:20.990
through the efficacy of 12 step,

1332
00:57:20.990 --> 00:57:23.800
which I know has overlap in the Venn diagram

1333
00:57:23.800 --> 00:57:26.475
with "The Course in Miracles" and your perspective.

1334
00:57:26.475 --> 00:57:27.650
Yeah, the 11th step, yeah.

1335
00:57:27.650 --> 00:57:28.900
This idea of...

1336
00:57:28.900 --> 00:57:31.180
You have strong feelings about reparations,

1337
00:57:31.180 --> 00:57:35.603
and the amends process is fundamental to recovery,

1338
00:57:36.670 --> 00:57:38.560
as is a spiritual connection

1339
00:57:39.510 --> 00:57:41.370
in a non-dogmatic way,

1340
00:57:41.370 --> 00:57:45.690
so when you look at rectifying

1341
00:57:45.690 --> 00:57:47.350
where we've gone off the rails

1342
00:57:48.330 --> 00:57:50.760
socially, politically, culturally,

1343
00:57:50.760 --> 00:57:54.460
there does seem to be a necessity

1344
00:57:54.460 --> 00:57:58.570
of inventorying those missteps

1345
00:57:58.570 --> 00:58:01.980
and actually implementing amends,

1346
00:58:01.980 --> 00:58:04.900
not just incremental policy change,

1347
00:58:04.900 --> 00:58:09.900
but how can we not only acknowledge the ills of our past

1348
00:58:10.360 --> 00:58:13.020
but also make them right

1349
00:58:13.020 --> 00:58:18.020
so that we can be whole as we move forward.

1350
00:58:18.530 --> 00:58:21.833
Well, the United States does need 12-stepping.

1351
00:58:22.770 --> 00:58:25.837
It needs to get out of its denial:

1352
00:58:25.837 --> 00:58:27.100
"I can handle this."

1353
00:58:27.100 --> 00:58:28.870
We've been going, "Can the Republicans handle it?

1354
00:58:28.870 --> 00:58:31.030
Can the Democrats handle it?

1355
00:58:31.030 --> 00:58:32.390
Which can manage this?"

1356
00:58:32.390 --> 00:58:34.937
The situation has become unmanageable.

1357
00:58:34.937 --> 00:58:37.760
(chuckles) My life has become unmanageable.

1358
00:58:37.760 --> 00:58:38.851
It's so true, right?

1359
00:58:38.851 --> 00:58:39.684
Yeah, absolutely.

1360
00:58:39.684 --> 00:58:40.630
Yeah, it's amazing.

1361
00:58:40.630 --> 00:58:42.070
And once again,

1362
00:58:42.070 --> 00:58:43.370
like in the 12-
"But I got it."

1363
00:58:43.370 --> 00:58:44.203
Yeah, "I got it."

1364
00:58:44.203 --> 00:58:47.027
You don't got this. Your best thinking got you here, right?

1365
00:58:47.027 --> 00:58:50.390
And we're relying on the people that created the problem

1366
00:58:50.390 --> 00:58:51.223
to solve it,

1367
00:58:51.223 --> 00:58:52.640
telling us, "Go home.

1368
00:58:52.640 --> 00:58:53.473
It'll be fine."

1369
00:58:53.473 --> 00:58:54.780
Oh, and that's so much a part of the way

1370
00:58:54.780 --> 00:58:57.470
the political-media-industrial complex operates.

1371
00:58:57.470 --> 00:59:00.710
We're supposed to think that the only people qualified

1372
00:59:00.710 --> 00:59:02.590
to lead us out of this ditch

1373
00:59:02.590 --> 00:59:07.400
are people who have had careers ensconced in the car,

1374
00:59:07.400 --> 00:59:10.740
driving the car that led us into this ditch.

1375
00:59:10.740 --> 00:59:13.620
They act like we need better political car mechanics.

1376
00:59:13.620 --> 00:59:15.660
No, the problem is we're on the wrong road,

1377
00:59:15.660 --> 00:59:16.730
but that's a separate issue.

1378
00:59:16.730 --> 00:59:18.763
Let's go back to the 12 steps.

1379
00:59:20.690 --> 00:59:23.260
The 12 steps is a program of amends, obviously.

1380
00:59:23.260 --> 00:59:24.760
You have to admit your character defects,

1381
00:59:24.760 --> 00:59:27.280
you have to admit them to another person,

1382
00:59:27.280 --> 00:59:30.340
and you have to seek, where possible, to make amends.

1383
00:59:30.340 --> 00:59:33.090
In the Catholic religion, this is what confession is.

1384
00:59:33.090 --> 00:59:33.923
You have to atone.

1385
00:59:33.923 --> 00:59:36.820
In the Jewish religion, it's what Yom Kippur is,

1386
00:59:36.820 --> 00:59:38.920
the holiest day of the year, the Day of Atonement.

1387
00:59:38.920 --> 00:59:41.510
You have to admit the exact nature of your wrongs

1388
00:59:41.510 --> 00:59:43.250
and seek to make amends.

1389
00:59:43.250 --> 00:59:46.140
Now, when it comes to reparations for me,

1390
00:59:46.140 --> 00:59:49.260
I have for years been at my lectures

1391
00:59:49.260 --> 00:59:51.140
doing these ritualized apologies.

1392
00:59:51.140 --> 00:59:53.340
In my book "Illuminata," I have the ritualized apologies

1393
00:59:53.340 --> 00:59:57.190
to Native Americans, blacks in America, et cetera,

1394
00:59:57.190 --> 01:00:02.190
but I came to realize that if you took $1,000 from me,

1395
01:00:03.020 --> 01:00:05.400
I would really appreciate the apology,

1396
01:00:05.400 --> 01:00:07.230
but (chuckles) I also want my money back,

1397
01:00:07.230 --> 01:00:08.430
and so it got to the point

1398
01:00:08.430 --> 01:00:10.010
where we can talk about white privilege.

1399
01:00:10.010 --> 01:00:12.410
We can talk about deconstructing our own racism,

1400
01:00:12.410 --> 01:00:14.000
but at this point, I feel it's time

1401
01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:16.910
to do more than atone for slavery.

1402
01:00:16.910 --> 01:00:18.880
It's time to do more than atone

1403
01:00:20.460 --> 01:00:24.980
for the 100 years of institutionalized oppression of blacks

1404
01:00:24.980 --> 01:00:28.320
that occurred after the 250 years of slavery.

1405
01:00:28.320 --> 01:00:31.220
It's time to make amends now,

1406
01:00:31.220 --> 01:00:33.610
and like you were saying,

1407
01:00:33.610 --> 01:00:36.290
the same psychological and spiritual principles

1408
01:00:36.290 --> 01:00:39.560
that prevail within the life of an individual

1409
01:00:39.560 --> 01:00:41.560
prevail within the life of a nation

1410
01:00:41.560 --> 01:00:44.120
because that's all a nation is is a group of people.

1411
01:00:44.120 --> 01:00:48.110
Germany has paid $89 billion in reparations

1412
01:00:48.110 --> 01:00:49.410
to Jewish organizations

1413
01:00:49.410 --> 01:00:50.670
since World War II,

1414
01:00:50.670 --> 01:00:52.830
and this has gone far

1415
01:00:52.830 --> 01:00:56.000
to create a kind of emotional reconciliation

1416
01:00:56.000 --> 01:00:59.180
between Germany and the Jews of Europe,

1417
01:00:59.180 --> 01:01:00.800
not only the full mea culpa,

1418
01:01:00.800 --> 01:01:02.520
which they certainly did,

1419
01:01:02.520 --> 01:01:05.110
but also two things:

1420
01:01:05.110 --> 01:01:09.423
reparations and the guarantee that in perpetuity,

1421
01:01:11.120 --> 01:01:12.950
school children in Germany

1422
01:01:12.950 --> 01:01:13.803
would learn the history of the Holocaust

1423
01:01:13.803 --> 01:01:16.400
so that they would understand how these things start,

1424
01:01:16.400 --> 01:01:18.980
and that's where the United States is.

1425
01:01:18.980 --> 01:01:22.000
We have not evolved on the level of consciousness

1426
01:01:22.000 --> 01:01:25.830
to realize we will not be moving forward the way we want

1427
01:01:25.830 --> 01:01:29.050
until we do make this change.

1428
01:01:29.050 --> 01:01:31.100
Look at the history here.

1429
01:01:31.100 --> 01:01:33.780
World War II was over in 1945,

1430
01:01:33.780 --> 01:01:36.420
and look how much Germany has cleaned up.

1431
01:01:36.420 --> 01:01:38.190
Global antisemitism is an issue again,

1432
01:01:38.190 --> 01:01:40.000
but not based on that.

1433
01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:41.203
They cleaned it up.

1434
01:01:42.290 --> 01:01:45.190
My gosh, the Civil War was over in the 1860s.

1435
01:01:45.190 --> 01:01:49.620
We are still passing this toxic baton

1436
01:01:49.620 --> 01:01:51.240
of systemic racism

1437
01:01:51.240 --> 01:01:54.550
and the reactions and the horrors

1438
01:01:56.600 --> 01:01:58.080
of this evil

1439
01:01:58.080 --> 01:01:59.890
and how it has infused too much

1440
01:01:59.890 --> 01:02:01.730
of our economic functioning, et cetera,

1441
01:02:01.730 --> 01:02:03.710
generation to generation to generation.

1442
01:02:03.710 --> 01:02:06.363
We could be the generation to clean it up.

1443
01:02:07.690 --> 01:02:10.260
Well, look, Germany can't make the Holocaust

1444
01:02:10.260 --> 01:02:11.470
not have occurred,

1445
01:02:11.470 --> 01:02:14.630
but with reparations and the level of mea culpa,

1446
01:02:14.630 --> 01:02:17.820
they've gone far towards beginning again,

1447
01:02:17.820 --> 01:02:22.220
and the United States could do the same.

1448
01:02:22.220 --> 01:02:24.470
I feel like we're very far from that, though.

1449
01:02:24.470 --> 01:02:27.530
Not that we're in denial of that reality,

1450
01:02:27.530 --> 01:02:29.360
but it's dismissed

1451
01:02:29.360 --> 01:02:32.210
as politically suicidal

1452
01:02:32.210 --> 01:02:36.070
and economically unfeasible

1453
01:02:36.070 --> 01:02:39.663
Okay, if I may, this is

1454
01:02:39.663 --> 01:02:42.930
because we have such a corrupt political establishment

1455
01:02:42.930 --> 01:02:44.800
that follows rather than leads.

1456
01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:47.170
That should be the point of leadership within any system

1457
01:02:47.170 --> 01:02:49.580
but particularly within political leadership,

1458
01:02:49.580 --> 01:02:52.030
that you build consensus.

1459
01:02:52.030 --> 01:02:54.420
My experience as a candidate,

1460
01:02:54.420 --> 01:02:57.870
I would go into all-white audiences

1461
01:02:57.870 --> 01:03:01.550
in states that had such a small black population

1462
01:03:01.550 --> 01:03:02.900
that most of the people in the room

1463
01:03:02.900 --> 01:03:07.010
hadn't even had a lot of relationships with black people.

1464
01:03:07.010 --> 01:03:08.310
Let's say it was in New Hampshire,

1465
01:03:08.310 --> 01:03:10.340
or let's say it was in Iowa or someplace like that.

1466
01:03:10.340 --> 01:03:11.173
I walk into the room.

1467
01:03:11.173 --> 01:03:14.300
This was my experience over and over and over again,

1468
01:03:14.300 --> 01:03:15.860
including among white people

1469
01:03:15.860 --> 01:03:18.010
in states like South Carolina, okay?

1470
01:03:18.010 --> 01:03:21.880
I go into the room, and the subject of reparations comes up.

1471
01:03:21.880 --> 01:03:24.630
The body language I'm getting from people is like this,

1472
01:03:26.040 --> 01:03:31.040
and then I give a little 10-minute-maximum thumbnail sketch

1473
01:03:31.690 --> 01:03:33.750
of the history of race in America.

1474
01:03:33.750 --> 01:03:37.070
The first slave ships came here in 1619.

1475
01:03:37.070 --> 01:03:40.090
There was almost 200 years

1476
01:03:41.080 --> 01:03:43.130
of slavery in this country.

1477
01:03:43.130 --> 01:03:45.830
At the end of the Civil War, historians believe,

1478
01:03:45.830 --> 01:03:48.660
there was anywhere between four to five million people

1479
01:03:48.660 --> 01:03:50.190
who were formerly enslaved.

1480
01:03:50.190 --> 01:03:53.380
Those people were promised 40 acres and a mule

1481
01:03:53.380 --> 01:03:57.020
for every former-slave family of four.

1482
01:03:57.020 --> 01:03:58.810
Most of the time, it was not given.

1483
01:03:58.810 --> 01:04:01.570
Even when it was given, it was then repatriated.

1484
01:04:01.570 --> 01:04:02.670
What were people to do?

1485
01:04:02.670 --> 01:04:05.410
You tell somebody, "You're not a slave any longer,"

1486
01:04:05.410 --> 01:04:07.560
but how were you supposed to make a living?

1487
01:04:08.412 --> 01:04:11.940
If you had that 40 acres and a mule, you could.

1488
01:04:11.940 --> 01:04:15.160
The North sent, during the years of Reconstruction,

1489
01:04:15.160 --> 01:04:18.350
federal troops to the South

1490
01:04:18.350 --> 01:04:21.420
to guarantee that slavery would not be reinstituted.

1491
01:04:21.420 --> 01:04:25.720
Once they left, many in the South had just held their breath

1492
01:04:25.720 --> 01:04:28.050
until the soldiers from the North were gone,

1493
01:04:28.050 --> 01:04:30.230
and then they passed the black code laws,

1494
01:04:30.230 --> 01:04:31.700
which would ensure

1495
01:04:31.700 --> 01:04:34.650
subpar economic, political, and social opportunity

1496
01:04:34.650 --> 01:04:35.660
for black people.

1497
01:04:35.660 --> 01:04:38.410
That lasted almost 100 years

1498
01:04:38.410 --> 01:04:40.070
until Martin Luther King.

1499
01:04:40.070 --> 01:04:43.780
We passed the Voting Rights Act 1964-1965.

1500
01:04:43.780 --> 01:04:46.610
The Voting Rights Act to give black people...

1501
01:04:46.610 --> 01:04:47.910
To ensure their voting rights,

1502
01:04:47.910 --> 01:04:49.990
which now the John Roberts court has gutted,

1503
01:04:49.990 --> 01:04:52.250
which is why we have all these voting-suppression efforts.

1504
01:04:52.250 --> 01:04:56.070
Passed the Civil Rights Act to dismantle segregation,

1505
01:04:56.070 --> 01:04:58.070
so you've got 300 years

1506
01:04:58.070 --> 01:05:00.030
of institutionalized violence

1507
01:05:00.030 --> 01:05:01.290
against black people.

1508
01:05:01.290 --> 01:05:03.850
Now, anybody would, I'm sure, agree

1509
01:05:03.850 --> 01:05:06.220
that if you've been kicking someone to the ground,

1510
01:05:06.220 --> 01:05:09.500
and certainly kicking someone to the ground for 350 years

1511
01:05:09.500 --> 01:05:10.920
is quite a bit of kicking,

1512
01:05:10.920 --> 01:05:13.100
you morally and ethically owe it to them

1513
01:05:13.100 --> 01:05:15.440
not just to stop kicking

1514
01:05:15.440 --> 01:05:17.640
but to help them get back up,

1515
01:05:17.640 --> 01:05:19.370
and if Martin Luther King had lived...

1516
01:05:19.370 --> 01:05:21.730
They had dealt with voting rights.

1517
01:05:21.730 --> 01:05:23.360
They had dealt with civil rights,

1518
01:05:23.360 --> 01:05:25.040
and they would have gotten to the issue

1519
01:05:25.040 --> 01:05:27.690
of closing that economic gap

1520
01:05:27.690 --> 01:05:29.370
that was understandable

1521
01:05:29.370 --> 01:05:31.100
between whites and black

1522
01:05:31.100 --> 01:05:34.120
at the end of the civil rights movement.

1523
01:05:34.120 --> 01:05:37.260
And we've never closed it, and it's simply time.

1524
01:05:37.260 --> 01:05:38.340
I would go through this.

1525
01:05:38.340 --> 01:05:41.780
I would talk about the history,

1526
01:05:41.780 --> 01:05:43.670
and many of the things that I just said to you...

1527
01:05:43.670 --> 01:05:46.440
I'm sure none of what I just said to you, Rich,

1528
01:05:46.440 --> 01:05:48.450
was news or a surprise to you,

1529
01:05:48.450 --> 01:05:50.630
but you'd be surprised how many Americans

1530
01:05:50.630 --> 01:05:52.280
I don't believe are racist in their heart

1531
01:05:52.280 --> 01:05:56.070
but are just under-informed and undereducated.

1532
01:05:56.070 --> 01:05:59.150
The point of my story is that I would go through...

1533
01:05:59.150 --> 01:06:00.840
That's what I just told you,

1534
01:06:00.840 --> 01:06:04.710
and people whose body language had been like this,

1535
01:06:04.710 --> 01:06:08.560
at the end, are jumping up on their chairs,

1536
01:06:08.560 --> 01:06:11.510
standing ovations: "We need reparations."

1537
01:06:11.510 --> 01:06:13.630
Don't pin this on the American people.

1538
01:06:13.630 --> 01:06:15.167
That's what the politicians do:

1539
01:06:15.167 --> 01:06:16.820
"Oh, the American people don't want it."

1540
01:06:16.820 --> 01:06:18.870
No, you mothers don't want it,

1541
01:06:18.870 --> 01:06:20.410
and you won't go there,

1542
01:06:20.410 --> 01:06:23.240
and if it is politically suicidal, lose your job.

1543
01:06:23.240 --> 01:06:26.280
Why do politicians think they're the only people

1544
01:06:26.280 --> 01:06:28.770
who have jobs where they have to make ethical decisions?

1545
01:06:28.770 --> 01:06:31.980
And if I make the ethical decision, I might lose my job.

1546
01:06:31.980 --> 01:06:34.710
What's the answer to that in an ethical society?

1547
01:06:34.710 --> 01:06:35.573
Lose your job.

1548
01:06:36.610 --> 01:06:39.253
Reparations is the right thing to do.

1549
01:06:42.100 --> 01:06:43.230
From my experience

1550
01:06:43.230 --> 01:06:44.310
having run for president

1551
01:06:44.310 --> 01:06:47.110
and having talked about this issue all over this country,

1552
01:06:47.110 --> 01:06:50.580
I believe that the decency of the American people,

1553
01:06:50.580 --> 01:06:52.730
the dignitency of the American people,

1554
01:06:52.730 --> 01:06:54.870
the basic sense of right and wrong and fairness

1555
01:06:54.870 --> 01:06:55.703
of the American people,

1556
01:06:55.703 --> 01:06:58.240
could, indeed, be harnessed for this purpose.

1557
01:06:58.240 --> 01:07:00.440
When you're talking about even $500 billion,

1558
01:07:01.790 --> 01:07:03.550
you need make people recognize

1559
01:07:05.390 --> 01:07:07.110
the parties move in lockstep

1560
01:07:07.110 --> 01:07:09.340
to give the military-industrial complex,

1561
01:07:09.340 --> 01:07:12.140
what, 780 billion every year,

1562
01:07:12.140 --> 01:07:15.050
so we have to just bust through these illusions

1563
01:07:15.050 --> 01:07:20.050
and these myths and these toxic lies

1564
01:07:20.235 --> 01:07:23.320
that hold progress at bay,

1565
01:07:23.320 --> 01:07:27.010
and race relations, I think, is just one of many examples.

1566
01:07:27.010 --> 01:07:28.903
Yeah, it's very beautifully put.

1567
01:07:30.289 --> 01:07:32.610
It reminds me of what we were talking about earlier,

1568
01:07:32.610 --> 01:07:34.190
this difference or dissonance

1569
01:07:34.190 --> 01:07:36.780
between voter sentiment

1570
01:07:36.780 --> 01:07:39.300
and the establishment

1571
01:07:39.300 --> 01:07:43.380
of the political infrastructure

1572
01:07:43.380 --> 01:07:44.980
that is recalcitrant

1573
01:07:44.980 --> 01:07:48.800
and dictates what voters want and don't want

1574
01:07:48.800 --> 01:07:51.870
but in a way that's disconnected from the truth of that.

1575
01:07:51.870 --> 01:07:53.543
On such a level.

1576
01:07:54.970 --> 01:07:58.820
On the subject of defense budgets,

1577
01:07:58.820 --> 01:08:01.870
another idea that you've proposed that I love

1578
01:08:01.870 --> 01:08:05.330
is this idea of a Department of Peace,

1579
01:08:05.330 --> 01:08:08.150
which, when you think about it, yeah, okay,

1580
01:08:08.150 --> 01:08:13.123
can be "oh, how woo woo," but actually,

1581
01:08:14.300 --> 01:08:17.440
wouldn't that be the most prophylactic

1582
01:08:17.440 --> 01:08:21.850
in terms of maintaining comity across the world,

1583
01:08:21.850 --> 01:08:24.128
comity, C-O-M-I-T-Y,

1584
01:08:24.128 --> 01:08:25.200
(Marianne chuckles)

1585
01:08:25.200 --> 01:08:27.970
prevent these young people

1586
01:08:27.970 --> 01:08:29.820
from becoming disenfranchised

1587
01:08:29.820 --> 01:08:31.060
and thus radicalized

1588
01:08:31.060 --> 01:08:33.483
and thus a national security risk.

1589
01:08:36.708 --> 01:08:39.939
How do you preserve cohesiveness

1590
01:08:39.939 --> 01:08:43.870
in our country and in other countries across the world

1591
01:08:43.870 --> 01:08:46.580
as an insurance policy against war,

1592
01:08:46.580 --> 01:08:47.413
to begin with,

1593
01:08:47.413 --> 01:08:50.610
which is much more expensive once we're waging it?

1594
01:08:50.610 --> 01:08:52.550
Unfortunately, American foreign policy

1595
01:08:52.550 --> 01:08:54.470
is not run or driven

1596
01:08:54.470 --> 01:08:57.823
by the idea of an effort to create comity within the world.

1597
01:08:59.083 --> 01:09:00.323
It's like medicine.

1598
01:09:01.260 --> 01:09:02.220
Of course.

1599
01:09:02.220 --> 01:09:04.280
It's basically about disease management

1600
01:09:05.250 --> 01:09:06.680
and treating symptoms

1601
01:09:06.680 --> 01:09:08.360
as opposed to being preventative.

1602
01:09:08.360 --> 01:09:11.240
Right, so let's talk about why that is though.

1603
01:09:11.240 --> 01:09:13.117
As John F. Kennedy said,

1604
01:09:13.117 --> 01:09:16.370
"We will end war, or war will end us."

1605
01:09:16.370 --> 01:09:18.800
The American foreign policy establishment is...

1606
01:09:18.800 --> 01:09:23.110
You look at $40 billion budget

1607
01:09:23.110 --> 01:09:24.280
for the State Department

1608
01:09:24.280 --> 01:09:28.530
versus the 780 billion-or-more budget

1609
01:09:28.530 --> 01:09:30.240
for the Defense Department.

1610
01:09:30.240 --> 01:09:34.750
Whereas the State Department used to drive

1611
01:09:34.750 --> 01:09:35.830
American foreign policy,

1612
01:09:35.830 --> 01:09:37.650
it doesn't not so much now.

1613
01:09:37.650 --> 01:09:41.510
Raytheon, Northrop Grumman, Boeing,

1614
01:09:41.510 --> 01:09:43.530
the defense contractors,

1615
01:09:43.530 --> 01:09:46.570
short-term profits for defense contractors

1616
01:09:46.570 --> 01:09:50.650
is what now drives our military policy.

1617
01:09:50.650 --> 01:09:53.823
If you do what you just said...

1618
01:09:53.823 --> 01:09:56.530
Statistically, we know what creates greater peace.

1619
01:09:56.530 --> 01:09:57.560
There are four factors

1620
01:09:57.560 --> 01:09:59.630
that create a higher incidence of peace

1621
01:09:59.630 --> 01:10:01.840
and a reduced incidence of violence:

1622
01:10:01.840 --> 01:10:04.530
expanded economic opportunities for women,

1623
01:10:04.530 --> 01:10:07.810
expanded educational opportunities for children,

1624
01:10:07.810 --> 01:10:10.270
the reduction of violence against women,

1625
01:10:10.270 --> 01:10:13.050
and the amelioration of unnecessary human despair.

1626
01:10:13.050 --> 01:10:14.710
Yeah, you're right.

1627
01:10:14.710 --> 01:10:16.690
You do that, you'd have a more peaceful world.

1628
01:10:16.690 --> 01:10:18.610
Where are the corporate profits there?

1629
01:10:18.610 --> 01:10:20.530
And that's all that this is about.

1630
01:10:20.530 --> 01:10:25.220
This is about a sick game of merchandising death.

1631
01:10:25.220 --> 01:10:29.107
We don't have universal access

1632
01:10:29.107 --> 01:10:30.810
to universal health care,

1633
01:10:30.810 --> 01:10:33.900
because of the profit-making factor

1634
01:10:33.900 --> 01:10:35.700
for health insurance companies

1635
01:10:35.700 --> 01:10:38.490
and big pharmaceutical companies.

1636
01:10:38.490 --> 01:10:41.380
We don't have anything near what we need

1637
01:10:41.380 --> 01:10:43.380
in terms of mitigating climate change,

1638
01:10:43.380 --> 01:10:46.120
because of short-term profits for fossil fuel companies.

1639
01:10:46.120 --> 01:10:49.810
And we don't have anything close to a foreign policy

1640
01:10:49.810 --> 01:10:53.690
that is driven by an agenda for peace

1641
01:10:53.690 --> 01:10:54.990
over the next 100 years,

1642
01:10:54.990 --> 01:10:57.600
because of profit-making factor

1643
01:10:57.600 --> 01:10:59.700
for the military-industrial complex.

1644
01:10:59.700 --> 01:11:02.820
And this is one of the ugliest monopolistic...

1645
01:11:02.820 --> 01:11:04.620
We talk about the corporate duopoly

1646
01:11:04.620 --> 01:11:06.090
of the political parties.

1647
01:11:06.090 --> 01:11:07.736
What's important is for us to realize the ways

1648
01:11:07.736 --> 01:11:08.800
in which they're not a duopoly.

1649
01:11:08.800 --> 01:11:09.780
They're a monopoly,

1650
01:11:09.780 --> 01:11:12.130
and one of the places where they are monopolistic

1651
01:11:12.130 --> 01:11:14.200
is in complete lockstep

1652
01:11:14.200 --> 01:11:16.080
with the military-industrial complex.

1653
01:11:16.080 --> 01:11:18.080
Course, they don't want a Department of Peace,

1654
01:11:18.080 --> 01:11:20.280
because a Department of Peace...

1655
01:11:22.335 --> 01:11:25.030
You wouldn't just have a military academy.

1656
01:11:25.030 --> 01:11:26.550
You'd also have a peace academy.

1657
01:11:26.550 --> 01:11:30.260
You'd have people who were resourced

1658
01:11:30.260 --> 01:11:33.680
in building peace, in peace-building measures.

1659
01:11:33.680 --> 01:11:35.330
When I was running for president,

1660
01:11:37.790 --> 01:11:39.610
all over the country, this would happen.

1661
01:11:39.610 --> 01:11:43.840
I would talk to people who were helping children

1662
01:11:43.840 --> 01:11:45.090
because this is where it all starts.

1663
01:11:45.090 --> 01:11:46.640
If you want peace in the world,

1664
01:11:47.950 --> 01:11:49.470
we need a massive front-ending.

1665
01:11:49.470 --> 01:11:51.790
I also want a Department of Children and Youth.

1666
01:11:51.790 --> 01:11:54.020
We need to massively front-end our resources

1667
01:11:54.020 --> 01:11:56.620
in the direction of people 10 years old and younger.

1668
01:11:57.460 --> 01:12:02.040
Now, the average American, I don't think, registers

1669
01:12:02.040 --> 01:12:04.860
how many millions of American children are food-insecure.

1670
01:12:04.860 --> 01:12:07.640
I don't think the average American registers

1671
01:12:07.640 --> 01:12:09.850
how many millions of Americans live in food deserts,

1672
01:12:09.850 --> 01:12:12.680
people who cannot get access to fresh fruits and vegetables.

1673
01:12:12.680 --> 01:12:14.080
How many of our obese children...

1674
01:12:14.080 --> 01:12:15.860
You know why these kids are obese?

1675
01:12:15.860 --> 01:12:18.430
Because their bodies keep trying

1676
01:12:18.430 --> 01:12:21.190
to get the necessary nourishment.

1677
01:12:21.190 --> 01:12:23.620
So they're actually under-nourished.

1678
01:12:23.620 --> 01:12:25.330
They're not over-nourished. They're under-nourished.

1679
01:12:25.330 --> 01:12:26.860
That's why they keep eating calories,

1680
01:12:26.860 --> 01:12:28.220
so they go, and they eat more M&amp;M'S,

1681
01:12:28.220 --> 01:12:31.726
or they eat more crap fast foods,

1682
01:12:31.726 --> 01:12:32.570
trying to get-

1683
01:12:32.570 --> 01:12:33.620
They live in food deserts

1684
01:12:33.620 --> 01:12:35.177
where healthy food is not available,

1685
01:12:35.177 --> 01:12:38.098
and the cheap low-hanging fruit is in the bodegas,

1686
01:12:38.098 --> 01:12:39.845
and that's what they're eating.

1687
01:12:39.845 --> 01:12:40.678
But this is where...

1688
01:12:40.678 --> 01:12:44.200
The corporate profits do not lie in helping them.

1689
01:12:44.200 --> 01:12:46.620
The survival of our democracy lies in helping them.

1690
01:12:46.620 --> 01:12:49.910
The survival of our species lies in helping them,

1691
01:12:49.910 --> 01:12:53.390
so just as we need to make a just transition

1692
01:12:53.390 --> 01:12:55.660
from a dirty economy to a clean economy,

1693
01:12:55.660 --> 01:12:57.550
we need to make a just transition

1694
01:12:57.550 --> 01:13:00.810
from a war economy to a peace economy.

1695
01:13:00.810 --> 01:13:02.320
And it's the same issue.

1696
01:13:02.320 --> 01:13:03.567
A lotta people would say,

1697
01:13:03.567 --> 01:13:05.900
"Why is it that these politicians continue

1698
01:13:05.900 --> 01:13:07.820
to walk in lockstep?"

1699
01:13:07.820 --> 01:13:10.850
In large part because of the jobs created

1700
01:13:10.850 --> 01:13:13.300
in their districts and in their states

1701
01:13:13.300 --> 01:13:15.423
by defense-related activities.

1702
01:13:16.370 --> 01:13:20.210
We spend hundreds of billions every year

1703
01:13:20.210 --> 01:13:23.580
over what even military leaders say is actually needed

1704
01:13:23.580 --> 01:13:25.690
for our military security,

1705
01:13:25.690 --> 01:13:29.100
but just as with a dirty economy,

1706
01:13:29.100 --> 01:13:31.640
the same talents and expertise

1707
01:13:31.640 --> 01:13:35.640
of research and development, manufacturing, et cetera,

1708
01:13:35.640 --> 01:13:37.930
can move in the direction of peace.

1709
01:13:37.930 --> 01:13:41.450
And it is also statistically true

1710
01:13:41.450 --> 01:13:43.940
that a peace economy where your investment is

1711
01:13:43.940 --> 01:13:47.220
in education, health care, economic opportunity, et cetera,

1712
01:13:47.220 --> 01:13:51.010
gives you more of an economic return on investment.

1713
01:13:51.010 --> 01:13:52.590
Raytheon ain't having it, though.

1714
01:13:52.590 --> 01:13:55.190
Oh, Raytheon is not having it,

1715
01:13:55.190 --> 01:13:56.373
but we have to have it.

1716
01:13:57.598 --> 01:13:58.800
We've got to say it.

1717
01:13:58.800 --> 01:14:00.050
We've got to stand on it.

1718
01:14:00.050 --> 01:14:01.170
We've got to run on it.

1719
01:14:01.170 --> 01:14:05.100
I love the idea, but ultimately,

1720
01:14:05.100 --> 01:14:10.100
do we not have to disentangle campaign finance laws

1721
01:14:10.820 --> 01:14:14.010
and find a way to (chuckles) prevent

1722
01:14:14.010 --> 01:14:16.520
this insane undue influence

1723
01:14:16.520 --> 01:14:20.423
that these industries have on legislatures?

1724
01:14:21.735 --> 01:14:23.617
It's anti-democratic in every-
It's the cancer underlying-

1725
01:14:23.617 --> 01:14:26.600
Yeah, and it's like, "Can't we all find some way

1726
01:14:26.600 --> 01:14:28.970
to fundamentally agree on that?"

1727
01:14:28.970 --> 01:14:31.108
Well, I think the American people do agree on it.

1728
01:14:31.108 --> 01:14:32.187
Sure, I think they do too.

1729
01:14:32.187 --> 01:14:35.040
But the undue influence of money on our politics,

1730
01:14:35.040 --> 01:14:36.430
particularly corporate money,

1731
01:14:36.430 --> 01:14:38.880
is the cancer underlying all the other cancers,

1732
01:14:38.880 --> 01:14:40.660
particularly dark money,

1733
01:14:40.660 --> 01:14:44.203
particularly that which has exploded since Citizens United.

1734
01:14:46.110 --> 01:14:48.070
We certainly need to repeal that,

1735
01:14:48.070 --> 01:14:50.130
but that's not gonna happen anytime soon.

1736
01:14:50.130 --> 01:14:53.640
Ultimately, we will need a constitutional amendment

1737
01:14:53.640 --> 01:14:57.370
that establishes public funding for federal campaigns.

1738
01:14:57.370 --> 01:14:58.700
I don't think most people realize

1739
01:14:58.700 --> 01:15:00.780
that your average congressman spends half their time

1740
01:15:00.780 --> 01:15:01.613
on the phone

1741
01:15:01.613 --> 01:15:02.446
trying to raise money.

1742
01:15:02.446 --> 01:15:04.815
Probably more than half their time.

1743
01:15:04.815 --> 01:15:06.470
It's so insane.
It starts on day one.

1744
01:15:06.470 --> 01:15:08.110
And yet these people, we're supposed to look at them

1745
01:15:08.110 --> 01:15:10.930
and go, "Oh, they're so qualified for leading us forward."

1746
01:15:10.930 --> 01:15:11.780
(Rich laughs)

1747
01:15:11.780 --> 01:15:13.430
It's the Ken on the Barbie dolls.

1748
01:15:14.970 --> 01:15:17.100
You were talking about the manner

1749
01:15:17.100 --> 01:15:21.000
in which money goes into...

1750
01:15:21.000 --> 01:15:23.360
The medicalization of-

1751
01:15:23.360 --> 01:15:25.210
The sickness-care system rather than the-

1752
01:15:25.210 --> 01:15:26.560
Yeah, exactly.

1753
01:15:26.560 --> 01:15:27.950
Yeah, we don't have a health care system.

1754
01:15:27.950 --> 01:15:28.783
We have a sickness-care-

1755
01:15:28.783 --> 01:15:32.510
But it's metastasized

1756
01:15:32.510 --> 01:15:34.917
into much more than that, right?

1757
01:15:34.917 --> 01:15:37.230
We've medicalized sadness and grief.

1758
01:15:37.230 --> 01:15:38.830
We're overmedicating everybody,

1759
01:15:38.830 --> 01:15:40.030
and that also speaks

1760
01:15:40.030 --> 01:15:41.590
to the undue influence

1761
01:15:41.590 --> 01:15:44.100
of these huge pharmaceutical companies

1762
01:15:44.100 --> 01:15:48.670
and their financial interests

1763
01:15:48.670 --> 01:15:51.170
in making sure that everybody is adequately medicated

1764
01:15:51.170 --> 01:15:52.430
at all times.
Absolutely, and that's

1765
01:15:52.430 --> 01:15:54.560
another reason they came after me, actually,

1766
01:15:54.560 --> 01:15:55.507
on the campaign.
Yeah, and that's

1767
01:15:55.507 --> 01:15:58.970
not to say that medication certainly does...

1768
01:15:58.970 --> 01:16:00.830
It has its place

1769
01:16:00.830 --> 01:16:01.960
in mental health.
Oh, of course, it does.

1770
01:16:01.960 --> 01:16:03.950
In appropriate situations,

1771
01:16:03.950 --> 01:16:08.950
but as somebody who understands very well the difference

1772
01:16:09.270 --> 01:16:13.810
between what one might consider clinical depression

1773
01:16:13.810 --> 01:16:17.930
versus grief or having a hard time

1774
01:16:17.930 --> 01:16:22.350
and the fact that we're now giving people pills

1775
01:16:22.350 --> 01:16:24.250
that just are going through something

1776
01:16:24.250 --> 01:16:26.530
that they need to go through

1777
01:16:26.530 --> 01:16:27.690
because we're human beings

1778
01:16:27.690 --> 01:16:29.320
and life is hard...

1779
01:16:29.320 --> 01:16:32.970
I look at antidepressants the way I look at painkillers.

1780
01:16:32.970 --> 01:16:34.860
They have a place, but we now know

1781
01:16:34.860 --> 01:16:37.220
the Sackler family, Purdue Pharmacy, et cetera...

1782
01:16:37.220 --> 01:16:39.440
We know about predatory behavior

1783
01:16:39.440 --> 01:16:41.340
on the part of pharmaceutical executives,

1784
01:16:41.340 --> 01:16:43.180
creating profit centers,

1785
01:16:43.180 --> 01:16:46.083
dangerous immoral profit centers,

1786
01:16:47.560 --> 01:16:49.200
where they do not belong.

1787
01:16:49.200 --> 01:16:52.010
And I think it is absolutely naive of us

1788
01:16:52.010 --> 01:16:54.660
to think that that's not happening

1789
01:16:54.660 --> 01:16:56.740
in relation to antidepressants as well,

1790
01:16:56.740 --> 01:16:59.430
and the fact that if you even suggest that,

1791
01:16:59.430 --> 01:17:01.940
you are considered naive or irresponsible

1792
01:17:02.997 --> 01:17:05.163
about mental health is absurd.

1793
01:17:06.374 --> 01:17:08.630
What's happening is how naive and irresponsible people are

1794
01:17:08.630 --> 01:17:11.730
to so blindly trust big pharmaceutical companies,

1795
01:17:11.730 --> 01:17:14.170
and like you said, they do wonderful things.

1796
01:17:14.170 --> 01:17:16.340
My God, I had surgery not long ago,

1797
01:17:16.340 --> 01:17:19.180
and believe me, I was grateful for those painkillers.

1798
01:17:19.180 --> 01:17:20.570
Of course, they have a place,

1799
01:17:20.570 --> 01:17:23.670
as do, I'm sure, in many people's lives, antidepressants,

1800
01:17:23.670 --> 01:17:27.460
but the fact that you can't even suggest

1801
01:17:27.460 --> 01:17:30.930
that the overprescription of medication in America

1802
01:17:30.930 --> 01:17:31.890
is a real issue

1803
01:17:31.890 --> 01:17:34.033
and we should be able to talk about it,

1804
01:17:36.150 --> 01:17:38.660
that has to do with the chokehold of big pharma

1805
01:17:38.660 --> 01:17:40.280
and the fact that the military,

1806
01:17:40.280 --> 01:17:41.420
excuse me, not the military

1807
01:17:41.420 --> 01:17:44.040
but the political system and the media,

1808
01:17:44.040 --> 01:17:46.343
like when Anderson Cooper came after me,

1809
01:17:48.307 --> 01:17:49.707
talking about that issue...

1810
01:17:49.707 --> 01:17:50.970
And I said, "Well, that's interesting

1811
01:17:50.970 --> 01:17:54.770
because look how many pharmaceutical companies advertise

1812
01:17:54.770 --> 01:17:56.030
on your television show."

1813
01:17:56.030 --> 01:17:58.310
And he said, "I don't know who advertises."

1814
01:17:58.310 --> 01:17:59.550
I wish I said to him-

1815
01:17:59.550 --> 01:18:01.990
It's constant pharma ads.

1816
01:18:01.990 --> 01:18:04.273
And by the way, before Ronald Reagan,

1817
01:18:05.560 --> 01:18:07.543
this was not legal.

1818
01:18:09.020 --> 01:18:12.630
Pharmaceutical companies could not advertise on television

1819
01:18:12.630 --> 01:18:13.730
before Ronald Reagan

1820
01:18:13.730 --> 01:18:15.080
and the orgy of deregulation

1821
01:18:15.080 --> 01:18:17.905
that his administration brought forth.

1822
01:18:17.905 --> 01:18:21.040
(tuts) Yeah, it's a sticky wicket.

1823
01:18:21.040 --> 01:18:23.140
It's all one and the same, though.

1824
01:18:23.140 --> 01:18:24.550
All of these issues go back

1825
01:18:24.550 --> 01:18:28.330
to this inextricable connectivity

1826
01:18:28.330 --> 01:18:32.153
between government and giant conglomerates.

1827
01:18:33.100 --> 01:18:34.848
And also you bring in on the sickness issue,

1828
01:18:34.848 --> 01:18:37.290
and one of the things I brought up in a debate was,

1829
01:18:37.290 --> 01:18:38.897
that we have to ask ourselves,

1830
01:18:38.897 --> 01:18:41.010
"Why is there so much more chronic illness

1831
01:18:41.010 --> 01:18:43.150
in the United States than among citizens

1832
01:18:43.150 --> 01:18:46.720
of other equally advanced, European, democratic societies,

1833
01:18:46.720 --> 01:18:47.553
for instance?"

1834
01:18:47.553 --> 01:18:48.980
This goes back, as you well know...

1835
01:18:48.980 --> 01:18:50.210
You talk about this.

1836
01:18:50.210 --> 01:18:52.070
This goes to our chemical policies,

1837
01:18:52.070 --> 01:18:53.730
our agricultural policies,

1838
01:18:53.730 --> 01:18:55.480
animal factory farming.

1839
01:18:55.480 --> 01:18:56.480
And subsidies.

1840
01:18:56.480 --> 01:18:58.410
Yeah, it's a whole corporate matrix.

1841
01:18:58.410 --> 01:19:00.620
We have this corporate aristocracy.

1842
01:19:00.620 --> 01:19:03.453
We have reverted to an aristocratic condition.

1843
01:19:04.570 --> 01:19:07.310
And we have to understand what that archetype means.

1844
01:19:07.310 --> 01:19:09.000
An aristocracy means

1845
01:19:09.000 --> 01:19:11.520
that a few people are considered entitled

1846
01:19:11.520 --> 01:19:13.690
to the major resources of the country.

1847
01:19:13.690 --> 01:19:15.617
We repudiated that in 1776,

1848
01:19:15.617 --> 01:19:18.300
and we need to repudiate again.

