Forgiveness means knowing that who we are is good.

2113
01:30:27.250 --> 01:30:29.243
Living on this earth, we forget that,

2114
01:30:30.240 --> 01:30:33.460
but when I look at you and I

2115
01:30:35.450 --> 01:30:38.450
base my perception of you only on your error,

2116
01:30:38.450 --> 01:30:39.793
only on your lovelessness,

2117
01:30:41.090 --> 01:30:44.370
then I am stuck within that realm of lovelessness.

2118
01:30:44.370 --> 01:30:46.487
And "The Course of Miracles" says,

2119
01:30:46.487 --> 01:30:49.140
"You are at the effect of the laws

2120
01:30:49.140 --> 01:30:52.310
that prevail within the world that you identify with."

2121
01:30:52.310 --> 01:30:54.470
If I'm willing to extend my perception

2122
01:30:54.470 --> 01:30:56.840
beyond what my physical senses perceive,

2123
01:30:56.840 --> 01:30:58.660
your error, your lovelessness,

2124
01:30:58.660 --> 01:31:01.210
to what I know to be true in you,

2125
01:31:01.210 --> 01:31:06.210
then I remind both you and myself what is true in us,

2126
01:31:06.310 --> 01:31:08.870
and the situation repairs.

2127
01:31:08.870 --> 01:31:11.513
And we're gonna have to do that on a larger level.

2128
01:31:12.660 --> 01:31:15.320
The hatred, the cynicism, the anger

2129
01:31:15.320 --> 01:31:16.830
on both the left and the right

2130
01:31:17.780 --> 01:31:20.490
dispels and deflects the possibility

2131
01:31:20.490 --> 01:31:22.140
for political miracles,

2132
01:31:22.140 --> 01:31:24.630
and we must open our hearts

2133
01:31:24.630 --> 01:31:28.210
and still passionately disagree, form boundaries.

2134
01:31:28.210 --> 01:31:30.070
Just like you have boundaries in personal relationships,

2135
01:31:30.070 --> 01:31:33.530
you have boundaries in political relationships,

2136
01:31:33.530 --> 01:31:34.900
but you can do all of that with love.

2137
01:31:34.900 --> 01:31:38.117
You can do all of that with respect and humility,

2138
01:31:38.117 --> 01:31:39.900
and to me, that's the portal

2139
01:31:41.440 --> 01:31:43.970
through which we can walk to a more sustainable world.

2140
01:31:43.970 --> 01:31:45.950
The resistance to forgive,

2141
01:31:45.950 --> 01:31:48.230
that impulse that we feel

2142
01:31:48.230 --> 01:31:51.610
when we sense that we've been wronged,

2143
01:31:51.610 --> 01:31:54.630
is ostensibly to shoulder a burden.

2144
01:31:54.630 --> 01:31:56.097
It's a self-punishment, right?

2145
01:31:56.097 --> 01:32:00.320
And there is a liberation or a freedom that happens

2146
01:32:00.320 --> 01:32:03.770
when you can develop the facility

2147
01:32:03.770 --> 01:32:06.100
to let go of it, to forgive,

2148
01:32:06.100 --> 01:32:07.457
as difficult as that might be.

2149
01:32:07.457 --> 01:32:12.457
And that forgiveness should be turned inward as well.

2150
01:32:12.740 --> 01:32:14.059
Self-forgiveness is

2151
01:32:14.059 --> 01:32:15.025
a big piece of that as well.
Well, you can't forgive

2152
01:32:15.025 --> 01:32:16.840
yourself if you don't forgive others.

2153
01:32:16.840 --> 01:32:17.673
That's why the course says,

2154
01:32:17.673 --> 01:32:20.050
"You become generous out of self-interest."

2155
01:32:20.050 --> 01:32:21.720
The course says when you're attacking someone,

2156
01:32:21.720 --> 01:32:23.650
blaming someone, imagining

2157
01:32:23.650 --> 01:32:27.250
that there is a sword falling down on their head...

2158
01:32:27.250 --> 01:32:29.730
But it's actually falling down on yours

2159
01:32:29.730 --> 01:32:30.950
because at the deepest level,

2160
01:32:30.950 --> 01:32:32.270
if you get into the metaphysic of it,

2161
01:32:32.270 --> 01:32:34.340
there's no place where you stop and I start.

2162
01:32:34.340 --> 01:32:36.100
None of us except enlightened masters

2163
01:32:36.100 --> 01:32:37.830
are perfect at any of this,

2164
01:32:37.830 --> 01:32:41.870
but even making the transforms our lives.

2165
01:32:41.870 --> 01:32:45.560
Yeah, we've all seen our soul elevated

2166
01:32:45.560 --> 01:32:47.930
by witnessing somebody forgive somebody

2167
01:32:47.930 --> 01:32:50.960
where logic would dictate that maybe they shouldn't,

2168
01:32:50.960 --> 01:32:52.790
and we understand fundamentally

2169
01:32:52.790 --> 01:32:56.630
that that is a noble act,

2170
01:32:56.630 --> 01:32:58.770
that that is nourishing.

2171
01:32:58.770 --> 01:33:00.150
And yet we're in a culture

2172
01:33:00.150 --> 01:33:03.030
where we're increasingly judging everybody

2173
01:33:03.030 --> 01:33:04.860
based on their worst day

2174
01:33:04.860 --> 01:33:06.580
and canceling people

2175
01:33:06.580 --> 01:33:08.060
and saying, "You go away now"

2176
01:33:08.060 --> 01:33:09.810
and "that's it for you."

2177
01:33:09.810 --> 01:33:11.380
There is no room,

2178
01:33:11.380 --> 01:33:13.683
at least in the social media space,

2179
01:33:14.941 --> 01:33:17.344
for that forgiveness,

2180
01:33:17.344 --> 01:33:19.900
and unless we find a way back to that,

2181
01:33:19.900 --> 01:33:22.267
a way to prioritize it

2182
01:33:22.267 --> 01:33:27.170
and inject it into our discourse and conduct,

2183
01:33:28.440 --> 01:33:29.490
we're lost.

2184
01:33:29.490 --> 01:33:30.420
You are so right.

2185
01:33:30.420 --> 01:33:32.580
I think you put it so well.

2186
01:33:32.580 --> 01:33:34.740
We're judging everybody according to their worst day

2187
01:33:34.740 --> 01:33:36.800
or their most stupid tweet.

2188
01:33:36.800 --> 01:33:38.610
Everything's "I gotcha."

2189
01:33:38.610 --> 01:33:40.320
It's terrible.

2190
01:33:40.320 --> 01:33:44.360
Many years ago, my best friend, who has since passed...

2191
01:33:44.360 --> 01:33:46.280
We were sitting in my bedroom,

2192
01:33:46.280 --> 01:33:48.060
and I was on the phone

2193
01:33:48.060 --> 01:33:50.550
with someone who worked for me,

2194
01:33:50.550 --> 01:33:52.490
and I started yelling at the guy.

2195
01:33:52.490 --> 01:33:54.697
I got off the phone, and Richard said to me,

2196
01:33:54.697 --> 01:33:56.125
"What was that?"

2197
01:33:56.125 --> 01:33:58.230
and I said, "Well, he did this" or "he didn't do that"

2198
01:33:58.230 --> 01:33:59.420
or whatever it was,

2199
01:33:59.420 --> 01:34:01.900
and Richard looked at me, and he went, "Marianne,

2200
01:34:01.900 --> 01:34:03.193
he made a mistake.

2201
01:34:05.340 --> 01:34:06.957
People make mistakes."

2202
01:34:10.886 --> 01:34:13.440
(sighs) It was a brick to my forehead I remember.

2203
01:34:13.440 --> 01:34:15.790
And no matter what he did,

2204
01:34:15.790 --> 01:34:17.220
the fact that you were such a bitch about it

2205
01:34:17.220 --> 01:34:18.772
makes you no better than...

2206
01:34:18.772 --> 01:34:20.113
(sighs) I got it.

2207
01:34:20.980 --> 01:34:22.910
I'm not 100% at practicing it

2208
01:34:22.910 --> 01:34:24.360
but a lot better than I used to be,

2209
01:34:24.360 --> 01:34:27.650
because people make mistakes.

2210
01:34:27.650 --> 01:34:31.160
Yeah, how do we try

2211
01:34:31.160 --> 01:34:33.717
to create space for that?

2212
01:34:33.717 --> 01:34:35.017
"The Course in Miracles" says you say,

2213
01:34:35.017 --> 01:34:37.947
"Dear God, I'm willing to see this differently."

2214
01:34:40.120 --> 01:34:43.313
The path that we are here to monitor is not somebody else.

2215
01:34:44.329 --> 01:34:45.888
It's like you were talking about AA.

2216
01:34:45.888 --> 01:34:48.270
You're not here to take somebody else's inventory.

2217
01:34:48.270 --> 01:34:51.630
The path you're here to monitor very vigilantly is your own.

2218
01:34:51.630 --> 01:34:54.120
Dear God, I see how self-righteous I am in this moment.

2219
01:34:54.120 --> 01:34:55.990
Dear God, I see how judgmental I am in this moment.

2220
01:34:55.990 --> 01:34:57.730
Dear God, I see how blaming.

2221
01:34:57.730 --> 01:34:59.150
Who do hell how do I think I am?

2222
01:34:59.150 --> 01:35:00.800
Dear God, take this away from me.

2223
01:35:02.540 --> 01:35:04.753
And I see this all the time.

2224
01:35:04.753 --> 01:35:06.630
Then what happens is

2225
01:35:06.630 --> 01:35:09.250
sometimes you realize "just keep your mouth shut.

2226
01:35:09.250 --> 01:35:11.440
There's nothing that even needs to be said."

2227
01:35:11.440 --> 01:35:13.660
Sometimes you realize "oh, there's something

2228
01:35:13.660 --> 01:35:16.240
that's gonna need to be communicated here,"

2229
01:35:16.240 --> 01:35:19.040
but you will communicate it from such a different place.

2230
01:35:19.990 --> 01:35:20.990
You will communicate it

2231
01:35:20.990 --> 01:35:23.533
from elegance and charity and compassion.

2232
01:35:25.332 --> 01:35:26.257
"The Course in Miracles" says,

2233
01:35:26.257 --> 01:35:28.300
"If you're judging and attacking someone,

2234
01:35:28.300 --> 01:35:30.829
you're wrong even if you're right."

2235
01:35:30.829 --> 01:35:34.208
(tuts) Right, but we have a social media ecosystem-

2236
01:35:34.208 --> 01:35:35.041
Oh yeah, we do.

2237
01:35:35.041 --> 01:35:37.210
That has a misalignment of incentives

2238
01:35:37.210 --> 01:35:38.890
because it's rewarding people

2239
01:35:38.890 --> 01:35:42.170
for that level of judgment and invective.

2240
01:35:42.170 --> 01:35:44.330
We do, but each and every one of us

2241
01:35:44.330 --> 01:35:47.800
can refuse to participate in that and do what we can,

2242
01:35:47.800 --> 01:35:51.170
because there's also some beautiful stuff on social media.

2243
01:35:51.170 --> 01:35:52.003
There's a line in the course

2244
01:35:52.003 --> 01:35:56.810
where it says, "Nothing in the world is unholy or holy,

2245
01:35:56.810 --> 01:36:00.230
except determined by its purpose,

2246
01:36:00.230 --> 01:36:01.830
what the mind is doing with it,"

2247
01:36:01.830 --> 01:36:04.290
and you can see incredible things, credible good,

2248
01:36:04.290 --> 01:36:06.130
that comes from social media,

2249
01:36:06.130 --> 01:36:09.610
and you can see terrible, even evil, things

2250
01:36:09.610 --> 01:36:11.160
that emerge from social media.

2251
01:36:11.160 --> 01:36:14.860
And it all gets back to the ethics and the principles

2252
01:36:14.860 --> 01:36:17.830
of right and wrong and enlightenment

2253
01:36:17.830 --> 01:36:21.830
that I do think so many of us are at least trying for.

2254
01:36:21.830 --> 01:36:23.740
Yeah, it's sometimes difficult

2255
01:36:23.740 --> 01:36:28.230
to understand the best move;

2256
01:36:28.230 --> 01:36:31.780
for example, (tuts) the other day,

2257
01:36:31.780 --> 01:36:35.410
Massie, that congressman, the guy from Kentucky

2258
01:36:35.410 --> 01:36:37.720
who posted the holiday photo

2259
01:36:37.720 --> 01:36:39.297
of his whole family-
"Jesus, send the ammo"?

2260
01:36:39.297 --> 01:36:40.547
(laughs) With the guns.

2261
01:36:41.490 --> 01:36:44.060
And I saw that, and I was so appalled.

2262
01:36:44.060 --> 01:36:46.450
We're days away from school shooting.

2263
01:36:46.450 --> 01:36:49.730
Normally, I don't mix it up on social media

2264
01:36:49.730 --> 01:36:53.070
and inject myself

2265
01:36:53.070 --> 01:36:56.250
into that kind of discussion or acrimony,

2266
01:36:56.250 --> 01:36:58.403
but I felt like I couldn't let it stand.

2267
01:36:59.461 --> 01:37:01.707
I tweeted it and said,

2268
01:37:01.707 --> 01:37:03.557
"I just feel like these people are...

2269
01:37:05.030 --> 01:37:06.130
It's difficult to imagine

2270
01:37:06.130 --> 01:37:08.950
how weak, insecure, and broken these people must be

2271
01:37:08.950 --> 01:37:12.180
to think that this is a good idea to share this photo."

2272
01:37:12.180 --> 01:37:13.100
It was met with a lot

2273
01:37:13.100 --> 01:37:17.030
of different (chuckles) opinions obviously,

2274
01:37:17.030 --> 01:37:20.440
and then I thought, "I probably shouldn't have tweeted that.

2275
01:37:20.440 --> 01:37:21.680
Why am I doing this?"

2276
01:37:21.680 --> 01:37:25.560
Or is there a responsibility

2277
01:37:25.560 --> 01:37:27.570
to say something

2278
01:37:28.670 --> 01:37:29.930
when somebody does something

2279
01:37:29.930 --> 01:37:31.903
that I feel is so deeply inappropriate?

2280
01:37:32.830 --> 01:37:34.410
Well, I think on that one,

2281
01:37:34.410 --> 01:37:36.320
and where I land on that one is,

2282
01:37:36.320 --> 01:37:37.350
that it's not about Massie.

2283
01:37:37.350 --> 01:37:39.560
It's about that school shooting in Michigan.

2284
01:37:39.560 --> 01:37:43.730
Within two days in Oakland County in Michigan,

2285
01:37:43.730 --> 01:37:47.560
due to credible threats of mass shootings,

2286
01:37:47.560 --> 01:37:50.900
every single public school in the county was closed.

2287
01:37:50.900 --> 01:37:52.490
Now, I raised my daughter in Michigan.

2288
01:37:52.490 --> 01:37:54.390
I have a lotta friends there.

2289
01:37:54.390 --> 01:37:55.830
There's an inflection point.

2290
01:37:55.830 --> 01:37:58.250
It's really interesting what's happening there.

2291
01:37:58.250 --> 01:38:01.100
A lot of people who would not necessarily have gone there,

2292
01:38:01.100 --> 01:38:04.310
since then, have said, "This gone too far."

2293
01:38:04.310 --> 01:38:07.180
Americans are afraid to send their kids to school,

2294
01:38:07.180 --> 01:38:08.530
but this is also an issue

2295
01:38:08.530 --> 01:38:10.170
where the consciousness of the American people

2296
01:38:10.170 --> 01:38:11.120
is not the problem.

2297
01:38:12.710 --> 01:38:14.470
Poll after poll shows

2298
01:38:14.470 --> 01:38:17.650
the American people want to close those loopholes.

2299
01:38:17.650 --> 01:38:19.630
Poll after poll shows the American people want

2300
01:38:19.630 --> 01:38:21.900
to outlaw bump stocks.

2301
01:38:21.900 --> 01:38:25.990
The polls show the American people want to rid our streets

2302
01:38:25.990 --> 01:38:27.640
of average citizens

2303
01:38:27.640 --> 01:38:29.860
who are carrying assault weapons,

2304
01:38:29.860 --> 01:38:31.970
AR-15s, AK-47s, et cetera.

2305
01:38:31.970 --> 01:38:34.170
This has to do with the chokehold

2306
01:38:34.170 --> 01:38:38.210
that the NRA and gun manufacturers has

2307
01:38:38.210 --> 01:38:39.410
on our Congress,

2308
01:38:39.410 --> 01:38:42.590
so it all goes back to money and politics.

2309
01:38:42.590 --> 01:38:43.970
But the idea

2310
01:38:43.970 --> 01:38:47.300
that right now a bogus interpretation

2311
01:38:47.300 --> 01:38:48.570
of the second amendment...

2312
01:38:48.570 --> 01:38:50.290
This is not about the second amendment.

2313
01:38:50.290 --> 01:38:52.690
This is about the money of gun manufacturers

2314
01:38:52.690 --> 01:38:54.070
and the hold that this holds

2315
01:38:54.070 --> 01:38:57.457
in terms of congressmen and senators who are told,

2316
01:38:57.457 --> 01:39:01.260
"If you vote for the most common-sense gun-safety law,

2317
01:39:01.260 --> 01:39:03.170
we're coming after you, and you're gonna lose your job."

2318
01:39:03.170 --> 01:39:06.170
And we need more of them will say, "Fine, I'll lose my job."

2319
01:39:07.480 --> 01:39:08.540
And right now...

2320
01:39:09.570 --> 01:39:11.350
I don't think a lotta people realize

2321
01:39:11.350 --> 01:39:13.060
the first official act of Donald Trump

2322
01:39:13.060 --> 01:39:14.320
when he became president

2323
01:39:14.320 --> 01:39:16.070
was to repeal a law

2324
01:39:16.070 --> 01:39:19.090
that kept violent criminals

2325
01:39:19.090 --> 01:39:20.540
from being able to buy a gun.

2326
01:39:21.714 --> 01:39:23.530
Yeah, I knew that.
The NRA will not be happy...

2327
01:39:23.530 --> 01:39:26.160
They even have little gun holsters in pink

2328
01:39:26.160 --> 01:39:27.253
for our little girls.

2329
01:39:29.730 --> 01:39:34.730
I know, so how do you maintain hope amidst all of this?

2330
01:39:35.510 --> 01:39:39.573
Because I believe that love prevails.

2331
01:39:40.760 --> 01:39:43.010
The crucifixion was followed by the resurrection.

2332
01:39:43.010 --> 01:39:45.210
The slavery in Egypt was followed

2333
01:39:45.210 --> 01:39:47.417
by deliverance to the Promised Land.

2334
01:39:47.417 --> 01:39:49.530
"The arc of the moral universe is long,

2335
01:39:49.530 --> 01:39:52.220
but it bends towards justice."

2336
01:39:52.220 --> 01:39:56.190
Even if, God forbid, there is a nuclear Holocaust

2337
01:39:56.190 --> 01:39:57.023
on this planet

2338
01:39:58.090 --> 01:40:00.913
and only five people are left,

2339
01:40:02.340 --> 01:40:04.440
those five will look at each other and go,

2340
01:40:05.277 --> 01:40:06.977
"Let's do it different this time."

2341
01:40:07.900 --> 01:40:08.923
It's gonna happen.

2342
01:40:09.850 --> 01:40:11.280
It's that symbolic three days

2343
01:40:11.280 --> 01:40:12.940
between the crucifixion and the resurrection,

2344
01:40:12.940 --> 01:40:14.850
the symbolic 40 years

2345
01:40:14.850 --> 01:40:16.240
between slavery in Egypt

2346
01:40:16.240 --> 01:40:17.990
and deliver into the Promised Land.

2347
01:40:19.210 --> 01:40:20.990
That is a sign.

2348
01:40:20.990 --> 01:40:22.890
There is a limited period of time.

2349
01:40:22.890 --> 01:40:25.050
What is up to free will

2350
01:40:25.050 --> 01:40:28.010
is will that be three years, three decades,

2351
01:40:28.010 --> 01:40:33.010
3,000 years, 30,000 years, lifetimes.

2352
01:40:33.100 --> 01:40:34.693
That is in our hands.

2353
01:40:38.490 --> 01:40:40.003
I believe in people.

2354
01:40:41.210 --> 01:40:44.400
It's economic systems and political systems

2355
01:40:44.400 --> 01:40:47.303
that are holding all this back right now,

2356
01:40:48.810 --> 01:40:50.780
but I believe that love will prevail,

2357
01:40:50.780 --> 01:40:53.180
because I believe that it always has.

2358
01:40:53.180 --> 01:40:54.013
It always will.

2359
01:40:54.013 --> 01:40:56.880
That's not only my religious and spiritual conviction.

2360
01:40:56.880 --> 01:40:58.804
It's my experience.

2361
01:40:58.804 --> 01:41:01.880
(tuts) I think that's a beautiful place to end it.

2362
01:41:01.880 --> 01:41:02.713
Thank you.

2363
01:41:02.713 --> 01:41:07.640
You are a powerful and magnificent human being.

2364
01:41:07.640 --> 01:41:08.500
I appreciate-

2365
01:41:08.500 --> 01:41:09.410
Thank you.

2366
01:41:09.410 --> 01:41:10.650
The work that you do.

2367
01:41:10.650 --> 01:41:12.360
The message and the vibration

2368
01:41:12.360 --> 01:41:13.660
that share with the world,

2369
01:41:16.140 --> 01:41:17.603
it is very powerful.

2370
01:41:18.500 --> 01:41:20.920
I guess the only thing left to ask you

2371
01:41:20.920 --> 01:41:23.203
is where are you taking this,

2372
01:41:23.203 --> 01:41:24.490
what is next for you,

2373
01:41:24.490 --> 01:41:26.403
or where are you placing your focus.

2374
01:41:27.330 --> 01:41:29.600
I think that there are these impulses

2375
01:41:29.600 --> 01:41:32.020
that are collective in the zeitgeist,

2376
01:41:32.020 --> 01:41:34.093
and I'm where everybody I else I know is,

2377
01:41:35.410 --> 01:41:37.960
where I bet, to some extent, you are,

2378
01:41:37.960 --> 01:41:39.293
everybody in this room is,

2379
01:41:40.210 --> 01:41:42.130
asking that question.

2380
01:41:42.130 --> 01:41:44.050
I think that's the question of the conscious person

2381
01:41:44.050 --> 01:41:46.650
right now: how can I best serve?

2382
01:41:46.650 --> 01:41:50.250
And we're living the question, living the inquiry,

2383
01:41:50.250 --> 01:41:52.970
me no less than everybody else I know.

2384
01:41:52.970 --> 01:41:56.510
But new connections are being made, ya know?

2385
01:41:56.510 --> 01:41:58.233
It's like an immune system, right?

2386
01:41:59.809 --> 01:42:02.930
The body survives

2387
01:42:02.930 --> 01:42:04.740
because there's an amazing amount

2388
01:42:05.700 --> 01:42:08.990
of assault and injury and illness that the body can take

2389
01:42:08.990 --> 01:42:11.380
as long as there's a healthy immune system.

2390
01:42:11.380 --> 01:42:13.233
I believe the psyche has an immune system.

2391
01:42:13.233 --> 01:42:16.620
It's amazing how much heartbreak and trauma we can take.

2392
01:42:16.620 --> 01:42:18.200
There's a psychic immune system,

2393
01:42:18.200 --> 01:42:21.820
and I believe there's an immune system in civilization

2394
01:42:21.820 --> 01:42:23.570
and the immune cells are awakening.

2395
01:42:24.580 --> 01:42:27.760
I remember I once fell down, cut my hands.

2396
01:42:27.760 --> 01:42:29.230
I was running, and I fell.

2397
01:42:29.230 --> 01:42:31.990
These huge gashes on my hands, it was so fascinating

2398
01:42:31.990 --> 01:42:33.850
to watch the wound 'cause it was right here,

2399
01:42:33.850 --> 01:42:35.487
and I remember a doctor friend of mine saying,

2400
01:42:35.487 --> 01:42:37.830
"You realize the red is good news.

2401
01:42:37.830 --> 01:42:39.320
It means all the white blood cells are rushing

2402
01:42:39.320 --> 01:42:40.840
to the wound,"

2403
01:42:40.840 --> 01:42:42.690
and that's what I feel is happening right now.

2404
01:42:42.690 --> 01:42:45.110
Everybody's rushing to the wound,

2405
01:42:45.110 --> 01:42:46.737
and cells in the body are assigned:

2406
01:42:46.737 --> 01:42:48.620
"You (snaps) go to the lungs.

2407
01:42:48.620 --> 01:42:50.330
You (snaps) go to the heart.

2408
01:42:50.330 --> 01:42:51.810
(snaps) You go to the bones,"

2409
01:42:51.810 --> 01:42:55.150
and right now we're all being assigned

2410
01:42:55.150 --> 01:42:56.760
to the area of the wound

2411
01:42:56.760 --> 01:42:58.700
where we can best make a difference.

2412
01:42:58.700 --> 01:43:00.810
And I know for myself and for most people I know,

2413
01:43:00.810 --> 01:43:02.190
we're not quite sure

2414
01:43:02.190 --> 01:43:04.010
where the assignment is right now,

2415
01:43:04.010 --> 01:43:05.830
but we can wake up every day

2416
01:43:05.830 --> 01:43:08.270
and do what we can to be the awakening.

2417
01:43:08.270 --> 01:43:11.757
Yeah, find the wound that speaks to you, right?

2418
01:43:11.757 --> 01:43:12.730
I feel like

2419
01:43:14.384 --> 01:43:16.270
(tuts) so many forms of new media,

2420
01:43:16.270 --> 01:43:18.360
like podcasting, et cetera,

2421
01:43:18.360 --> 01:43:20.680
play such a vital role in this.

2422
01:43:20.680 --> 01:43:22.410
It's providing so many people

2423
01:43:22.410 --> 01:43:24.540
with different avenues

2424
01:43:24.540 --> 01:43:26.280
for learning and exploring media

2425
01:43:26.280 --> 01:43:28.650
that just weren't available not that long ago,

2426
01:43:28.650 --> 01:43:30.350
and I feel like that's a big piece

2427
01:43:31.653 --> 01:43:35.296
in the construction of this strong immune system.

2428
01:43:35.296 --> 01:43:37.533
Absolutely, because traditional media...

2429
01:43:37.533 --> 01:43:40.500
It's so corporatized and bought and sold

2430
01:43:40.500 --> 01:43:42.300
it's that predetermined agenda,

2431
01:43:42.300 --> 01:43:44.080
and this is independent media,

2432
01:43:44.080 --> 01:43:46.450
people having a deeper conversation.

2433
01:43:46.450 --> 01:43:48.057
It was Werner Erhard who said,

2434
01:43:48.057 --> 01:43:50.520
"You can live your life from circumstances,

2435
01:43:50.520 --> 01:43:52.580
or you can live your life from a vision"

2436
01:43:52.580 --> 01:43:54.870
and things such as you're doing

2437
01:43:54.870 --> 01:43:59.020
allow us to have a vision of what's possible,

2438
01:43:59.020 --> 01:44:01.203
and from that, anything is possible.

